# vectorisation: a counted innermost loop over arrays becomes, where a runtime test admits it, one copy or fill of
# the bytes it moves, or a loop over vectors of the lanes the build's units hold followed by the loop for the rest
#
# a loop is taken when it is counted (`mirl.pass.analysis.induction`) by a compare of its stepping parameter itself,
# stepping by one, against a bound it does not define, staying while `iv < bound`, `bound > iv` or `iv != bound`
# (signed or unsigned), its header holding only that compare and its branch, and its one other block, the latch,
# holding only the step and accesses through element addresses `ptr.index(base, index)` of a base the loop does not
# define, each element of the access's own size, and the integer operations that compute their indices. the step is
# read by the branch back and otherwise only to compute indices (`a[i + 1]` sharing the step `i + 1`), so no
# lane of it is needed. nothing volatile or kept takes part. a function that states `scalar` is left alone. a secret
# takes part as any other value, its secrecy kept on every vector made of it and every access made in a scalar one's
# place stating what that one stated.
#
# an index is affine in the stepping parameter: the latch computes it from the stepping parameter, constants and
# values the loop does not define by sums, differences, products by a constant and shifts by a constant, each of the
# stepping parameter's type, so it is `stride * iv + rest`, `rest` the same on every trip. the stride is in elements.
# a stride of one walks the array one element a trip, and the stream's origin, the element address of its base at
# `rest`, is made once ahead of the loop (ahead of the outermost loop around it that defines none of `rest`'s values
# and is entered by one edge), so the vector loop and the tests index the origin by the stepping parameter alone. a
# stride of any other number reads lanes that lie apart, which needs a strided or gathering access: the ir states
# none, so no unit serves one, and a loop holding such a stream is left alone by that rule. an index of the stepping
# parameter alone keeps its base as its origin and makes nothing.
#
# the proofs below hold with an origin: the trips are the stepping parameter's alone; the stream's element at trip
# `t` is at `origin + t * size`, the address the latch's access at that trip reads, so every vector access covers
# exactly the addresses of its trips' accesses, at the alignment each of them stated; and two streams of one size lie
# the same bytes apart on every trip, their origins' difference, which is what each overlap test reads.
#
# what is known of two streams before the loop runs decides their overlap without a test: two streams in distinct
# objects (`mirl.pass.analysis.memory.apart`: two slots, or two globals that nothing elsewhere may stand for) never
# share an element, and two of one base whose indices differ by a constant lie that many elements
# apart on every trip, a stream against itself at the same index none, where a lane reads its element before the
# same lane writes it, as the trip did. only a pair neither settles gets a test on its addresses. a test reads what
# tells the two addresses apart, each base at its constant and the terms the other index does not share, which lie
# as far apart as the streams do, and for a copy the trips, and is made ahead of the outermost loop around the loop
# taken that defines none of them, so a nest tests once where its operands are fixed and not on every entry of the
# inner loop.
#
# a copy loop loads one element of a source and stores it to the same element of a destination. a fill loop stores
# one value the loop does not define whose bytes are all one byte: any byte, or a constant integer or float whose
# encoding is as wide as its type's size and is one byte repeated (a float zero among them), so that its store writes
# that byte to every byte of the element in any byte order. ahead of
# the header the loop is entered through new blocks: where the loop runs at least one trip (its own compare of the
# start against the bound), a copy of `trip * size` bytes from the start of the source to the start of the
# destination, or a fill of them, stands for the loop, unless the destination lies past the source by between one
# byte and the length less one, where the forward element loop would read an element an earlier trip wrote and so
# differs from a copy. after it the header is entered with the bound as its stepping parameter, so the loop runs no
# trip and every reader after it reads what it read before. otherwise the header is entered as before. a copy is
# stated `ascending` (`mirl.ir.metadata.Flags`): with the destination at or below the source, or apart from it, an
# upward copy gives what the loop gave. how the bytes move is the bulk legalisation's.
#
# a lanewise loop loads elements of its streams, computes operations of the latch over them and values the loop does
# not define, and stores one element. each operation gives each lane from the same lane of its operands, never traps
# and reads no memory: a lanewise one (`lanewise`), a conversion keeping each lane's value (a zero or sign extension,
# an integer's conversion to a float), or a comparison, whose condition only an accumulator's select reads. a loop
# that loads nothing and stores a value it does not define that no fill writes is one too: each vector stores the
# splat of that value, every lane the bytes a trip stored.
#
# every vector of the loop holds the trip's lanes, one lane per trip: the most lanes of the loop's narrowest lane type
# the function's code holds on its widest unit (`mirl.target.vector.split_for`), a power of two of at least two, halved
# until every step the vector loop forms is computed packed. so a widening makes the vector holding sixteen bytes the
# pieces holding sixteen lanes of the wider type, or the loop takes fewer lanes a trip, except that a loop storing
# nothing whose steps only widen, select and reduce is taken at the full count or not at all (`reduces_only`). each
# step is asked as the vector legalisation takes it for the same function on the same basis, after the served check's
# verdict, so nothing the pass forms is split back into scalar operations (`served_step`): over the runs of its widest
# lane type, each a whole piece of its result, each operand's run cut by a packed shuffle from a wider piece holding
# it, and a unit computing the operation at its lane types holding the run of each (`mirl.target.vector.packed`,
# `holds_for`), by a row the unit does not mark expanded (`mirl.target.vector.direct`): an operation served by a
# sequence of three or more instructions packs, and a program writing it keeps it packed, but without a cost model a
# loop formed on it is no gain. each splat of a value the loop does not define, each accumulator's reduction and every
# stream's vector held in pieces are asked the same way, an expanded row admitted, as each is taken once outside the
# trip or is the legalisation's own cut. a conversion no unit computes at its run goes through a wider integer
# (`route`): an extension of an extension of one kind is that extension, and a float conversion of a value-keeping
# extension gives what the conversion gives. a comparison is formed with its mask sign extended to integer lanes as
# wide as those compared, the language's mask of all ones and zeros, as the latch states it: the canonical form puts a
# compare's constant on its right (`mirl.opt.algebraic`) and runs again over the legal ir, so a comparison exchanged to
# a form a unit computes would be exchanged back. streams of elements of two sizes walk apart at different paces, so
# they are taken only where they are apart. the target must carry out an access below its type's alignment, since a
# vector access states only its element's.
# where a trip runs and the trips round down to a whole number of vectors are at least one vector, and no stream it
# loads lies below the one it stores by one byte up to a vector's bytes less one (where a lane would read what an
# earlier lane of its own vector wrote), a vector loop runs those trips, each lane doing what one trip did, the values
# the loop does not define splat to every lane once ahead of it, and then the header is entered with the index the
# vector loop reached, so the loop runs the trips left. with the destination at or below a source, a vector reads
# nothing an earlier element wrote that the loop would not have read, and with it a vector or more above, every
# element a vector reads was written, if at all, by an earlier vector.
#
# every other header parameter of a lanewise loop must be an accumulator: the latch reads it once, in a lanewise
# operation combining it with one other value, whose result only the branch back reads, and the operation regroups
# exactly (integer sum, product, and, or, exclusive or) or is a float sum or product in a build that permits float
# reassociation (`mirl.pass.relaxation`). without that permission a float sum keeps its order and the loop is left
# alone. or the branch back passes a select, by a comparison of the latch, between the parameter and its integer sum,
# or or exclusive or with one other value, read by nothing else: the trip combines `select(c, v, 0)`, zero being the
# operation's identity, which the vector loop forms as `and(v, m)` of the comparison's mask sign extended to v's lanes,
# all ones where c holds and zero where it does not (`accumulated`), so a lane whose condition fails combines the
# identity and is not skipped. a loop may then store nothing. the vector loop carries a vector of partial values per
# accumulator, every lane starting at the operation's identity (a float sum's negative zero, so a sum of negative zeros
# stays negative), and after it the lanes are reduced (`reduce.add` and the rest, `reduce.fadd.any` for a float sum)
# and combined with what the accumulator held before, which the header takes. a run shorter than a vector never enters
# the vector loop, so it gives exactly what the loop gave.
#
# rules: 1 to 6 of design section 5 are not relied on. the pass makes a branch on the arrays' addresses and changes
# how long the code takes, so it declares `Time.guards` and decides in a function that requires constant time what
# the function's proof accepts. the proof is the walk over the emitted code, and it trusts what the code states: the
# access statements, the frame's extents, the public ranges of slots and the callees' declarations. there:
# - the bulk form is never taken, since a copy or fill over a length the run decides is a secret's copy where the
#   bytes are secret, and the walk refuses it.
# - a loop is taken only where every value a branch the pass makes reads is public: the start, the bound and every
#   base and term of a stream, which the trip test, the rounding test and the overlap tests read. the vector loop's
#   own branch reads the stepping parameter and the end the trips round down to, made of those. no reduction or
#   comparison of the loop decides a branch: an accumulator is reduced after the vector loop and its comparisons only
#   mask a sum.
# - every vector the loop holds and every operation it forms is asked through the function's requirement
#   (`split_for`, `holds_for`, `packed`, `direct`), which answers lane by lane wherever the target's rows are not
#   timed relative to the lanes under the modes the function's code is read under, so an operation the walk would
#   time on a value is never formed and the loop stays scalar on that target.
# - each vector access states what the scalar access it stands for stated (`as_origin`), covering exactly the bytes
#   of its trips, so the access statements stay true, and with them every public range of a slot the trips wrote.
#   the pass makes no slot and no call, so the frame's extents and the callees' declarations do not change.
#
# cost: per loop one look at its header and latch and their uses, one walk of the memory analysis per pair of streams
# of distinct bases, and a constant number of instructions made per stream of a loop it takes. it reads the loops, the
# inductions and the memory analysis of the function.

use std.types.bool.bool;
use std.types.bool.false;
use std.types.bool.true;
use std.types.error.err;
use std.types.option.opt;
use std.types.result.res;
use std.types.size.usize;
use std.types.view.View;

use std.allocator;
use std.allocator.arena;
use std.collections.slice.Slice;
use std.collections.vector;

use mirl.build.builder;
use mirl.fold.word;
use mirl.ir.block.BlockData;
use mirl.ir.body;
use mirl.ir.cfg.graph.NONE;
use mirl.ir.cfg.loops;
use mirl.ir.cfg.loops.Loops;
use mirl.ir.function.Body;
use mirl.ir.function.ConstantTime;
use mirl.ir.function.in_constant_time;
use mirl.ir.id.Block;
use mirl.ir.id.Function;
use mirl.ir.id.Instruction;
use mirl.ir.id.NO_INSTRUCTION;
use mirl.ir.id.Value;
use mirl.ir.instruction.Branch;
use mirl.ir.instruction.InstructionData;
use mirl.ir.instruction.Place;
use mirl.ir.instruction.Request;
use mirl.ir.metadata.Flags;
use mirl.ir.metadata.NO_FLAGS;
use mirl.ir.module;
use mirl.ir.opcode.row.Immediate;
use mirl.ir.opcode.row.Opcode;
use mirl.ir.opcode.row.Row;
use mirl.ir.opcode.table;
use mirl.ir.type.format.Binary;
use mirl.ir.type.format.Format;
use FormatRow:  mirl.ir.type.format.Row;
use format_row: mirl.ir.type.format.row;
use type_table: mirl.ir.type.table;
use mirl.ir.type.table.Type;
use mirl.ir.value.Declaration;
use mirl.ir.value.Def;
use mirl.ir.value.ValueData;
use mirl.legal.emit;
use mirl.legal.emit.Site;
use mirl.pass.analysis;
use mirl.pass.analysis.induction;
use mirl.pass.analysis.induction.Counted;
use mirl.pass.analysis.induction.Inductions;
use mirl.pass.analysis.memory;
use mirl.pass.analysis.memory.Memory;
use mirl.pass.cache;
use mirl.pass.record.Context;
use mirl.pass.record.Ground;
use mirl.pass.record.Kind;
use mirl.pass.record.Pass;
use mirl.pass.record.Scope;
use mirl.pass.record.Time;
use mirl.pass.record.Unit;
use mirl.pass.record.did;
use mirl.pass.refusal;
use mirl.pass.refusal.edit;
use mirl.pass.relaxation;
use mirl.target.basis;
use mirl.target.capability;
use mirl.target.capability.LaneType;
use mirl.target.layout;
use mirl.target.layout.Layout;
use TargetError: mirl.target.record.Error;
use units:       mirl.target.vector;
use mirl.target.vector.Split;

# the pass: it adds blocks and moves an edge, so it keeps no analysis
pub val VECTORISE: Pass = Pass{name: "vectorise", kind: Kind.optimise{}, scope: Scope.function{visit}, needs: analysis.OF_LOOPS | analysis.OF_INDUCTIONS | analysis.OF_MEMORY, preserves: cache.NONE, time: Time.breaks{}, applies: physical, counts: "loops vectorised"};

# whether a target's addresses are numbers, so an element address is a byte offset from its base
fun physical(g: *Ground) bool {
    ret sel g.t.caps.addressing.physical;
}

# one value of an index the loop does not define, times a constant
# ---
# value: the value
# times: what it is multiplied by, never zero, at the stepping parameter's width
rec Term {
    value: Value;
    times: u64;
}

# an index as the latch computes it, `stride * iv + sum(times * value) + constant`, every number at the stepping
# parameter's width, wrapping as the index does
# ---
# stride:   what the stepping parameter is multiplied by, in elements
# terms:    the values the loop does not define, each once
# constant: the constant added
rec Affine {
    stride:   u64;
    terms:    vector.Vector[Term];
    constant: u64;
}

# an array the loop walks one element a trip
# ---
# base:    the address the latch indexes, which the loop does not define
# index:   the index the latch computes, of stride one
# indexed: the type the element address states, whose stride is the element's size
# size:    the element's size in bytes
# align:   the alignment its accesses state
# origin:  the element address of the base at the index's part the loop does not define, which the stepping parameter
#          indexes, once `adjust` made it
rec Stream {
    base:    Value;
    index:   Affine;
    indexed: Type;
    size:    u64;
    align:   u64;
    origin:  Value;
}

# a loop the pass may take
# ---
# head:     its header
# latch:    its other block
# iv:       the stepping parameter, by its position among the header's
# word:     its type, an integer as wide as the pointer
# bound:    the value it is compared with
# compare:  the compare's opcode
# left:     the stepping parameter is the compare's first operand
# entering: the terminator of the one edge into the header from outside the loop
# edge:     that edge's position among the terminator's
# start:    what that edge passes the stepping parameter
# step:     the latch's sum of the stepping parameter and one
rec Shape {
    head:     Block;
    latch:    Block;
    iv:       u32;
    word:     Type;
    bound:    Value;
    compare:  Opcode;
    left:     bool;
    entering: Instruction;
    edge:     u32;
    start:    Value;
    step:     Value;
}

# what the latch's accesses are
# ---
# loads:  each load: its stream and its result
# stores: each store: its stream and the value it stores
# ops:    each lanewise operation, in the order the latch holds them
rec Accesses {
    loads:  vector.Vector[Access];
    stores: vector.Vector[Access];
    ops:    vector.Vector[Instruction];
}

# one access of the latch
# ---
# stream: the array
# value:  what a load gives or a store writes
# at:     the access
rec Access {
    stream: Stream;
    value:  Value;
    at:     Instruction;
}

# one run over a function
# ---
# c:      the run
# f:      the function
# l:      its loops
# layout: the target's data layout of the module's types
# mem:    its memory analysis
# a:      storage for one loop's lists
rec Run {
    c:      *Context;
    f:      Function;
    l:      *Loops;
    layout: Layout;
    mem:    *Memory;
    a:      *allocator.Allocator;
}

fun body_of(x: *Run) *Body {
    ret ?x.c.m.functions.data[x.f].body;
}

fun no_values() Slice[Value] {
    ret Slice[Value]{data: nil, size: 0};
}

fun no_immediates() Slice[Immediate] {
    ret Slice[Immediate]{data: nil, size: 0};
}

# whether value `v` stands outside loop `n`: a constant, or a parameter or result of a block the loop does not hold
fun outside(x: *Run, n: u32, v: Value) bool {
    val b:   *Body = body_of(x);
    val def: Def   = b.values.data[v].def;
    if (sel def.constant)  { ret true; }
    if (sel def.parameter) { ret !loops.contains(x.l, n, def.parameter.block); }
    if (sel def.result) {
        val place: Place = b.instructions.data[def.result.instruction].place;
        if (sel place.placed) { ret !loops.contains(x.l, n, place.placed); }
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether an instruction reads or writes no memory, traps never and nothing reads its results, so a copy of the
# loop may go without it
fun idle(b: *Body, i: Instruction) bool {
    val d:       *InstructionData = ?b.instructions.data[i];
    val opt_row: opt[*Row]        = table.at(d.opcode);
    if (sel opt_row.none) { ret false; }
    val r: *Row = opt_row.some;
    if (r.effects.reads || r.effects.writes || r.terminator) { ret false; }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < d.results.len) {
        if (b.values.data[d.results.data[k]].uses.len != 0) { ret false; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret true;
}

# whether an instruction carries nothing the pass may not copy or drop: no volatile or kept mark
fun plain(b: *Body, i: Instruction) bool {
    val d: *InstructionData = ?b.instructions.data[i];
    ret !d.metadata.flags.volatile && !d.metadata.flags.kept;
}

# the alignment an access states, the layout's alignment of its type where it states none
fun alignment_of(x: *Run, d: *InstructionData, ty: Type) opt[u64] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < d.immediates.len) {
        val m: Immediate = d.immediates.data[i];
        if (sel m.alignment) { ret opt[u64].some{m.alignment}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val res_align: res[u64, TargetError] = layout.align(?x.layout, ty, type_table.DEFAULT_SPACE);
    if (sel res_align.err) { ret opt[u64].none{}; }
    ret opt[u64].some{res_align.ok};
}

# the bits of an integer type, zero for any other type
fun integer_bits(x: *Run, ty: Type) u32 {
    val res_shape: res[type_table.Shape, type_table.Error] = type_table.shape(?x.c.m.types, ty);
    if (sel res_shape.err)           { ret 0; }
    if (!(sel res_shape.ok.integer)) { ret 0; }
    ret res_shape.ok.integer.width;
}

# whether a type is a scalar integer or float, the types an element of a stream may be
fun scalar(x: *Run, ty: Type) bool {
    val res_shape: res[type_table.Shape, type_table.Error] = type_table.shape(?x.c.m.types, ty);
    if (sel res_shape.err) { ret false; }
    ret sel res_shape.ok.integer || sel res_shape.ok.float;
}

# a number at a width of `bits`, the bits above it clear
fun wrapped(x: u64, bits: u32) u64 {
    if (bits >= 64) { ret x; }
    ret x & ((1::u64 << bits::u64) - 1);
}

# add `times` of value `v` to an index's terms, a term whose multiplier comes to zero leaving them
fun add_term(a: *Affine, v: Value, times: u64, bits: u32) err[refusal.Error] {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < a.terms.len) {
        if (a.terms.data[k].value == v) {
            val sum: u64 = wrapped(a.terms.data[k].times + times, bits);
            if (sum == 0) {
                a.terms.data[k] = a.terms.data[a.terms.len - 1];
                a.terms.len     = a.terms.len - 1;
            }
            or { a.terms.data[k].times = sum; }
            ret err[refusal.Error].ok{};
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    if (times == 0) { ret err[refusal.Error].ok{}; }
    val res_pushed: res[usize, allocator.Error] = vector.push[Term](?a.terms, Term{value: v, times: times});
    if (sel res_pushed.err) { ret err[refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_pushed.err}}; }
    ret err[refusal.Error].ok{};
}

# whether an operation is one an index is computed by: a sum, a difference, a product or a left shift
fun index_op(op: Opcode) bool {
    ret op == table.ADD || op == table.SUB || op == table.MUL || op == table.SHL;
}

# the most operations an index is followed through
val DEPTH: u32 = 16;

# add `times` of value `v` to index `into`: the stepping parameter, a constant, a value the loop does not define, or
# an operation of the latch over them, a sum, a difference, a product by a constant or a left shift by a constant
# below the width, each of the stepping parameter's type. false where `v` is none of them
fun indexed_by(x: *Run, n: u32, s: *Shape, v: Value, times: u64, depth: u32, into: *Affine) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    val b:    *Body = body_of(x);
    val bits: u32   = integer_bits(x, s.word);
    if (bits == 0 || depth > DEPTH || !type_table.same(b.values.data[v].type, s.word)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    if (v == b.blocks.data[s.head].parameters.data[s.iv]) {
        into.stride = wrapped(into.stride + times, bits);
        ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{true};
    }
    val opt_known: opt[u64] = emit.known_in(x.c.m, b, v);
    if (sel opt_known.some) {
        into.constant = wrapped(into.constant + times * opt_known.some, bits);
        ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{true};
    }
    if (outside(x, n, v)) {
        val err_added: err[refusal.Error] = add_term(into, v, times, bits);
        if (sel err_added.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{err_added.err}; }
        ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{true};
    }
    val def: Def = b.values.data[v].def;
    if (!(sel def.result)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    val i:     Instruction      = def.result.instruction;
    val d:     *InstructionData = ?b.instructions.data[i];
    val place: Place            = d.place;
    if (!(sel place.placed))                       { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    if (d.operands.len != 2 || d.results.len != 1) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    if (place.placed != s.latch || !plain(b, i))   { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    val left:      Value    = d.operands.data[0];
    val right:     Value    = d.operands.data[1];
    val opt_left:  opt[u64] = emit.known_in(x.c.m, b, left);
    val opt_right: opt[u64] = emit.known_in(x.c.m, b, right);
    if (d.opcode == table.ADD || d.opcode == table.SUB) {
        val res_left: res[bool, refusal.Error] = indexed_by(x, n, s, left, times, depth + 1, into);
        if (sel res_left.err) { ret res_left; }
        if (!res_left.ok)     { ret res_left; }
        var by: u64 = times;
        if (d.opcode == table.SUB) { by = wrapped(0 - times, bits); }
        ret indexed_by(x, n, s, right, by, depth + 1, into);
    }
    if (d.opcode == table.MUL) {
        if (sel opt_right.some) { ret indexed_by(x, n, s, left, wrapped(times * opt_right.some, bits), depth + 1, into); }
        if (sel opt_left.some)  { ret indexed_by(x, n, s, right, wrapped(times * opt_left.some, bits), depth + 1, into); }
    }
    if (d.opcode == table.SHL) {
        if (sel opt_right.some) {
            if (opt_right.some < bits::u64) { ret indexed_by(x, n, s, left, wrapped(times << opt_right.some, bits), depth + 1, into); }
        }
    }
    ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false};
}

# whether every reader of value `v` computes an index of an element address in the latch: the index of a `ptr.index`
# or an index operation (`index_op`) of the stepping parameter's type whose own readers do, so the vector loop needs
# no lane of it
fun addressing(x: *Run, s: *Shape, v: Value, depth: u32) bool {
    if (depth > DEPTH) { ret false; }
    val b: *Body = body_of(x);
    var u: usize = 0;
    for (u < b.values.data[v].uses.len) {
        if (!addresses(x, s, b.values.data[v].uses.data[u].instruction, v, depth)) { ret false; }
        u = u + 1;
    }
    ret true;
}

# whether reader `i` of value `v` computes an index of an element address in the latch, as `addressing` asks of each
fun addresses(x: *Run, s: *Shape, i: Instruction, v: Value, depth: u32) bool {
    val b:       *Body            = body_of(x);
    val d:       *InstructionData = ?b.instructions.data[i];
    val place:   Place            = d.place;
    val indexes: bool             = d.opcode == table.PTR_INDEX && d.operands.len == 2 && d.operands.data[1] == v && d.operands.data[0] != v;
    if (!(sel place.placed))                                             { ret false; }
    if (place.placed != s.latch)                                         { ret false; }
    if (indexes)                                                         { ret true; }
    if (!index_op(d.opcode) || d.results.len != 1)                       { ret false; }
    if (!type_table.same(b.values.data[d.results.data[0]].type, s.word)) { ret false; }
    ret addressing(x, s, d.results.data[0], depth + 1);
}

# the stream an element address of the latch walks, none where it is no `ptr.index(base, index)` of a base the loop
# does not define, an index `indexed_by` follows and an element of `ty`'s size
fun stream_of(x: *Run, n: u32, s: *Shape, address: Value, ty: Type, access: *InstructionData) res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error] {
    val b:   *Body = body_of(x);
    val def: Def   = b.values.data[address].def;
    if (!(sel def.result)) { ret res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Stream].none{}}; }
    val i: Instruction      = def.result.instruction;
    val d: *InstructionData = ?b.instructions.data[i];
    if (d.opcode != table.PTR_INDEX || d.operands.len != 2 || d.immediates.len < 1) { ret res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Stream].none{}}; }
    if (!outside(x, n, d.operands.data[0]) || !plain(b, i))                         { ret res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Stream].none{}}; }
    val imm: Immediate = d.immediates.data[0];
    if (!(sel imm.ty)) { ret res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Stream].none{}}; }
    val res_space: res[u32, type_table.Error] = type_table.space(?x.c.m.types, b.values.data[d.operands.data[0]].type);
    if (sel res_space.err) { ret res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Stream].none{}}; }
    val res_stride: res[u64, TargetError] = layout.stride(?x.layout, imm.ty, res_space.ok);
    val res_size:   res[u64, TargetError] = layout.size(?x.layout, ty, res_space.ok);
    if (sel res_stride.err)                               { ret res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Stream].none{}}; }
    if (sel res_size.err)                                 { ret res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Stream].none{}}; }
    if (res_size.ok == 0 || res_stride.ok != res_size.ok) { ret res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Stream].none{}}; }
    val opt_align: opt[u64] = alignment_of(x, access, ty);
    if (sel opt_align.none) { ret res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Stream].none{}}; }
    var index:     Affine                   = Affine{stride: 0, terms: vector.init[Term](x.a), constant: 0};
    val res_index: res[bool, refusal.Error] = indexed_by(x, n, s, d.operands.data[1], 1, 0, ?index);
    if (sel res_index.err) { ret res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error].err{res_index.err}; }
    if (!res_index.ok)     { ret res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Stream].none{}}; }
    # a stride other than one element needs a strided or gathering access, which the ir states none of
    if (index.stride != 1) { ret res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Stream].none{}}; }
    ret res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Stream].some{Stream{base: d.operands.data[0], index: index, indexed: imm.ty, size: res_size.ok, align: opt_align.some, origin: d.operands.data[0]}}};
}

# the shape of loop `n` where it is one the pass may take
fun shape_of(x: *Run, ind: *Inductions, n: u32) opt[Shape] {
    val b:    *Body = body_of(x);
    val head: Block = loops.loop(x.l, n).header;
    if (head == 0) { ret opt[Shape].none{}; }
    val blocks: Slice[u32] = loops.body(x.l, n);
    if (blocks.size != 2) { ret opt[Shape].none{}; }
    val opt_counted: opt[Counted] = induction.counted(ind, n);
    if (sel opt_counted.none) { ret opt[Shape].none{}; }
    val ct: Counted = opt_counted.some;
    if (ct.next || ct.leaves) { ret opt[Shape].none{}; }
    if (sel ct.start.none)    { ret opt[Shape].none{}; }
    val staying: bool = (ct.left && (ct.compare == table.LT_U || ct.compare == table.LT_S)) || (!ct.left && (ct.compare == table.GT_U || ct.compare == table.GT_S)) || ct.compare == table.NE;
    if (!staying) { ret opt[Shape].none{}; }
    val st: induction.Step = ind.steps.data[ct.step];
    if (st.step != 1) { ret opt[Shape].none{}; }
    var latch: Block = blocks.data[0];
    if (latch == head) { latch = blocks.data[1]; }
    val latches: Slice[u32] = loops.latches(x.l, n);
    if (latches.size != 1 || latches.data[0] != latch) { ret opt[Shape].none{}; }
    if (b.blocks.data[latch].parameters.len != 0)      { ret opt[Shape].none{}; }

    # the header: the compare, its branch, and nothing anything reads
    val cbr:     Instruction = b.blocks.data[head].last;
    val compare: Value       = b.instructions.data[cbr].operands.data[0];
    var i:       Instruction = b.blocks.data[head].first;
    for (i != NO_INSTRUCTION) {
        if (i != cbr) {
            val d:          *InstructionData = ?b.instructions.data[i];
            val is_compare: bool             = d.results.len == 1 && d.results.data[0] == compare;
            if (!is_compare && !idle(b, i)) { ret opt[Shape].none{}; }
            if (!plain(b, i))               { ret opt[Shape].none{}; }
        }
        i = b.instructions.data[i].next;
    }

    val opt_entry: opt[Entry] = entering_of(x, n);
    if (sel opt_entry.none) { ret opt[Shape].none{}; }
    # the pass makes the trip count a value, the index the header is entered with after the loop and a bulk run's
    # length, so a secret bound would pass a public index a secret, which no edge does
    if (b.values.data[ct.bound].secret && !b.values.data[st.value].secret) { ret opt[Shape].none{}; }
    val word: Type = b.values.data[st.value].type;
    ret opt[Shape].some{Shape{head: head, latch: latch, iv: st.index, word: word, bound: ct.bound, compare: ct.compare, left: ct.left, entering: opt_entry.some.terminator, edge: opt_entry.some.edge, start: ct.start.some, step: st.next}};
}

# the one edge into a loop's header from outside the loop
# ---
# terminator: the terminator it leaves
# edge:       its position among the terminator's
rec Entry {
    terminator: Instruction;
    edge:       u32;
}

# the edge into loop `n`'s header from outside it, none where there is not exactly one
fun entering_of(x: *Run, n: u32) opt[Entry] {
    val b:     *Body      = body_of(x);
    val head:  Block      = loops.loop(x.l, n).header;
    val hd:    *BlockData = ?b.blocks.data[head];
    var found: opt[Entry] = opt[Entry].none{};
    var q:     usize      = 0;
    for (q < hd.predecessors.len) {
        val t:     Instruction = hd.predecessors.data[q].instruction;
        val place: Place       = b.instructions.data[t].place;
        if (sel place.placed && !loops.contains(x.l, n, place.placed)) {
            var e: usize = 0;
            for (e < b.instructions.data[t].edges.len) {
                if (b.instructions.data[t].edges.data[e].block == head) {
                    if (sel found.some && (found.some.terminator != t || found.some.edge != e::u32)) { ret opt[Entry].none{}; }
                    found = opt[Entry].some{Entry{terminator: t, edge: e::u32}};
                }
                e = e + 1;
            }
        }
        q = q + 1;
    }
    ret found;
}

# the outermost loop around loop `n`, `n` included, that defines none of `values`, every loop from `n` out to it
# entered by one edge: a computation of them made ahead of that loop's edge in runs once where it would run on every
# entry of `n`
fun placement(x: *Run, n: u32, values: Slice[Value]) u32 {
    var at:   u32  = n;
    var more: bool = true;
    for (more) {
        val up: u32 = loops.loop(x.l, at).parent;
        more = up != NONE;
        var k: usize = 0;
        for (more && k < values.size) {
            more = outside(x, up, values.data[k]);
            k    = k + 1;
        }
        if (more) {
            val opt_entry: opt[Entry] = entering_of(x, up);
            more = sel opt_entry.some;
        }
        if (more) { at = up; }
    }
    ret at;
}

# of two loops around the loop taken, the one deeper in the nest, which the other holds or is
fun deeper(x: *Run, a: u32, b: u32) u32 {
    if (loops.loop(x.l, a).depth >= loops.loop(x.l, b).depth) { ret a; }
    ret b;
}

# whether the stepping parameter is as wide as a pointer the streams' bases are
fun pointer_wide(x: *Run, s: *Shape, base: Value) bool {
    val res_size: res[u64, TargetError] = layout.size(?x.layout, body_of(x).values.data[base].type, type_table.DEFAULT_SPACE);
    if (sel res_size.err) { ret false; }
    ret integer_bits(x, s.word)::u64 == res_size.ok * 8;
}

# whether every reader of value `v` stands in the latch
fun kept_in_latch(x: *Run, s: *Shape, v: Value) bool {
    val b: *Body = body_of(x);
    var u: usize = 0;
    for (u < b.values.data[v].uses.len) {
        val place: Place = b.instructions.data[b.values.data[v].uses.data[u].instruction].place;
        if (!(sel place.placed))     { ret false; }
        if (place.placed != s.latch) { ret false; }
        u = u + 1;
    }
    ret true;
}

# whether an operation computes each lane from the same lane of its operands alone, never traps and reads no memory,
# so its vector form gives in each lane what the scalar one gave
fun lanewise(op: Opcode) bool {
    ret op == table.ADD || op == table.SUB || op == table.MUL || op == table.AND || op == table.OR || op == table.XOR || op == table.NEG || op == table.NOT || op == table.FADD || op == table.FSUB || op == table.FMUL || op == table.FDIV || op == table.FNEG;
}

# whether an instruction is lanewise: a lanewise operation, or a left shift by a constant below the width, which
# shifts each lane by the same count and so gives in each lane what the scalar one gave (the canonical form of a
# product by a power of two, `mirl.opt.algebraic`)
fun lanewise_at(x: *Run, b: *Body, d: *InstructionData) bool {
    if (lanewise(d.opcode))                           { ret true; }
    if (d.opcode != table.SHL || d.operands.len != 2) { ret false; }
    val opt_count: opt[u64] = emit.known_in(x.c.m, b, d.operands.data[1]);
    if (sel opt_count.none) { ret false; }
    ret opt_count.some < integer_bits(x, b.values.data[d.operands.data[0]].type)::u64;
}

# whether an instruction of one result is an operation the vector loop may carry: a lanewise one of one or two
# operands, a conversion (`conversion`) of one, a comparison (`comparison`) of two scalars, or a select of three, which
# `plan` takes only where it chooses an accumulator's next value
fun carried_op(x: *Run, b: *Body, d: *InstructionData) bool {
    if (d.results.len != 1)   { ret false; }
    if (lanewise_at(x, b, d)) { ret d.operands.len == 1 || d.operands.len == 2; }
    if (conversion(d.opcode)) { ret d.operands.len == 1 && scalar(x, b.values.data[d.operands.data[0]].type); }
    if (comparison(d.opcode)) { ret d.operands.len == 2 && scalar(x, b.values.data[d.operands.data[0]].type); }
    ret d.opcode == table.SELECT && d.operands.len == 3;
}

# the latch's accesses onto `into`, false where it holds anything but them, their element addresses and the
# operations computing the indices, operations the vector loop may carry (`carried_op`), the step and the branch back
fun accesses(x: *Run, n: u32, s: *Shape, into: *Accesses) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    val b:    *Body       = body_of(x);
    val last: Instruction = b.blocks.data[s.latch].last;
    if (b.instructions.data[last].opcode != table.BR) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    var i: Instruction = b.blocks.data[s.latch].first;
    for (i != last) {
        val d: *InstructionData = ?b.instructions.data[i];
        if (!plain(b, i)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        if (d.opcode == table.LOAD && d.operands.len == 1 && d.results.len == 1) {
            val ty: Type = b.values.data[d.results.data[0]].type;
            if (!scalar(x, ty) || !kept_in_latch(x, s, d.results.data[0])) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            val res_stream: res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error] = stream_of(x, n, s, d.operands.data[0], ty, d);
            if (sel res_stream.err)     { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_stream.err}; }
            if (sel res_stream.ok.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            val res_pushed: res[usize, allocator.Error] = vector.push[Access](?into.loads, Access{stream: res_stream.ok.some, value: d.results.data[0], at: i});
            if (sel res_pushed.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_pushed.err}}; }
        }
        or (d.opcode == table.STORE && d.operands.len == 2) {
            val ty: Type = b.values.data[d.operands.data[1]].type;
            if (!scalar(x, ty)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            val res_stream: res[opt[Stream], refusal.Error] = stream_of(x, n, s, d.operands.data[0], ty, d);
            if (sel res_stream.err)     { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_stream.err}; }
            if (sel res_stream.ok.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            val res_pushed: res[usize, allocator.Error] = vector.push[Access](?into.stores, Access{stream: res_stream.ok.some, value: d.operands.data[1], at: i});
            if (sel res_pushed.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_pushed.err}}; }
        }
        or (d.opcode == table.PTR_INDEX && d.operands.len == 2) {
            # an element address, which `stream_of` reads where an access reads it
            if (!kept_in_latch(x, s, d.results.data[0])) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        }
        or (d.results.len == 1 && d.results.data[0] == s.step) {
            if (d.opcode != table.ADD) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        }
        or (index_op(d.opcode) && d.results.len == 1 && addressing(x, s, d.results.data[0], 0)) {
            # an operation computing an index, which `stream_of` follows where an access reads the index
        }
        or (carried_op(x, b, d)) {
            if (!scalar(x, b.values.data[d.results.data[0]].type) || !kept_in_latch(x, s, d.results.data[0])) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            val res_pushed: res[usize, allocator.Error] = vector.push[Instruction](?into.ops, i);
            if (sel res_pushed.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_pushed.err}}; }
        }
        or (!idle(b, i)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        i = b.instructions.data[i].next;
    }
    # the step is read by the branch back once and otherwise only to compute indices, as `a[i + 1]` reads it, which a
    # stream's affine index already carries, so the vector loop needs no lane of it
    val sv:    *ValueData = ?b.values.data[s.step];
    var backs: usize      = 0;
    var u:     usize      = 0;
    for (u < sv.uses.len) {
        if (sv.uses.data[u].instruction == last)                      { backs = backs + 1; }
        or (!addresses(x, s, sv.uses.data[u].instruction, s.step, 0)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        u = u + 1;
    }
    ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{backs == 1};
}

# end the block the builder is at in a branch to a block, passing arguments
fun jump(st: *Site, to: Block, arguments: Slice[Value]) {
    var targets: [1]Branch = [1]Branch{Branch{block: to, arguments: arguments}};
    builder.emit(?st.bld, Request{opcode: table.BR, operands: no_values(), immediates: no_immediates(), targets: Slice[Branch]{data: ?targets[0], size: 1}});
}

# end the block the builder is at in a branch on a condition
fun fork(st: *Site, condition: Value, yes: Block, yes_args: Slice[Value], no: Block, no_args: Slice[Value]) {
    var ops:     [1]Value  = [1]Value{condition};
    var targets: [2]Branch = [2]Branch{Branch{block: yes, arguments: yes_args}, Branch{block: no, arguments: no_args}};
    builder.emit(?st.bld, Request{opcode: table.CBR, operands: Slice[Value]{data: ?ops[0], size: 1}, immediates: no_immediates(), targets: Slice[Branch]{data: ?targets[0], size: 2}});
}

# the element address of an address at index `at`, in the form the loop states it
fun indexing(st: *Site, base: Value, indexed: Type, at: Value) Value {
    var ops: [2]Value     = [2]Value{base, at};
    var imm: [1]Immediate = [1]Immediate{Immediate.ty{indexed}};
    ret builder.value(?st.bld, Request{opcode: table.PTR_INDEX, operands: Slice[Value]{data: ?ops[0], size: 2}, immediates: Slice[Immediate]{data: ?imm[0], size: 1}, targets: Slice[Branch]{data: nil, size: 0}});
}

# the element address of a stream at trip `at`, its origin indexed by it
fun element(st: *Site, s: Stream, at: Value) Value {
    ret indexing(st, s.origin, s.indexed, at);
}

# point the builder ahead of the edge into loop `at`: the edge `s` states for the loop taken, read before it moves
fun ahead(x: *Run, st: *Site, s: *Shape, n: u32, at: u32) err[refusal.Error] {
    builder.plain(?st.bld);
    if (at == n) {
        builder.before(?st.bld, s.entering);
        ret err[refusal.Error].ok{};
    }
    val opt_entry: opt[Entry] = entering_of(x, at);
    if (sel opt_entry.none) { ret err[refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.reason{"a loop the vectoriser places a computation ahead of has no one edge in"}}; }
    builder.before(?st.bld, opt_entry.some.terminator);
    ret err[refusal.Error].ok{};
}

# whether an index holds a term of the same value and multiplier
fun shares(a: *Affine, t: Term) bool {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < a.terms.len) {
        if (a.terms.data[k].value == t.value && a.terms.data[k].times == t.times) { ret true; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# a place made ahead of a loop
# ---
# value: what was made
# at:    the loop ahead of whose edge in it stands
rec Placed {
    value: Value;
    at:    u32;
}

# the element address of a stream's base at its index's constant and every term `skip` does not share, made ahead of
# the loop `placement` finds for the base and those terms. with `skip` empty it is the stream's origin; with the other
# stream of a pair, the two answers lie as far apart as the streams do, and read no term the two share, so a test of
# them is made where only what differs between them is fixed. an address of no term and no constant is the base
# itself, and makes nothing. the builder is left where it was not, so the caller points it again
fun partial(x: *Run, st: *Site, s: *Shape, n: u32, a: *Stream, skip: *Affine) res[Placed, refusal.Error] {
    val res_values: res[*Value, allocator.Error] = allocator.zallocate[Value](x.a, a.index.terms.len + 1);
    if (sel res_values.err) { ret res[Placed, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_values.err}}; }
    res_values.ok[0] = a.base;
    var count: usize = 1;
    var k:     usize = 0;
    for (k < a.index.terms.len) {
        if (!shares(skip, a.index.terms.data[k])) {
            res_values.ok[count] = a.index.terms.data[k].value;
            count                = count + 1;
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    if (count == 1 && a.index.constant == 0) { ret res[Placed, refusal.Error].ok{Placed{value: a.base, at: placement(x, n, Slice[Value]{data: res_values.ok, size: 1})}}; }
    val at:        u32                = placement(x, n, Slice[Value]{data: res_values.ok, size: count});
    val err_ahead: err[refusal.Error] = ahead(x, st, s, n, at);
    if (sel err_ahead.err) { ret res[Placed, refusal.Error].err{err_ahead.err}; }
    var sum:  Value = 0;
    var some: bool  = false;
    k = 0;
    for (k <= a.index.terms.len) {
        var part: opt[Value] = opt[Value].none{};
        if (k < a.index.terms.len) {
            val t: Term = a.index.terms.data[k];
            if (!shares(skip, t)) {
                part = opt[Value].some{t.value};
                if (t.times != 1) {
                    val res_times: res[Value, refusal.Error] = emit.word_constant(st, s.word, t.times);
                    if (sel res_times.err) { ret res[Placed, refusal.Error].err{res_times.err}; }
                    part = opt[Value].some{emit.binary(st, table.MUL, t.value, res_times.ok)};
                }
            }
        }
        or (a.index.constant != 0) {
            val res_constant: res[Value, refusal.Error] = emit.word_constant(st, s.word, a.index.constant);
            if (sel res_constant.err) { ret res[Placed, refusal.Error].err{res_constant.err}; }
            part = opt[Value].some{res_constant.ok};
        }
        if (sel part.some) {
            if (some) { sum = emit.binary(st, table.ADD, sum, part.some); }
            or        { sum = part.some; }
            some = true;
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret res[Placed, refusal.Error].ok{Placed{value: indexing(st, a.base, a.indexed, sum), at: at}};
}

# make a stream's origin (`partial` of no term skipped)
fun adjust(x: *Run, st: *Site, s: *Shape, n: u32, a: *Stream) err[refusal.Error] {
    var none:     Affine                     = Affine{stride: 0, terms: vector.init[Term](x.a), constant: 0};
    val res_made: res[Placed, refusal.Error] = partial(x, st, s, n, a, ?none);
    if (sel res_made.err) { ret err[refusal.Error].err{res_made.err}; }
    a.origin = res_made.ok.value;
    ret err[refusal.Error].ok{};
}

# the overlap test of a stored stream against a loaded one (`overlapping`), of the addresses `partial` makes of each
# against the other, made ahead of the deeper of their two loops and of `also`, a loop the caller's other operands fix
fun tested(x: *Run, st: *Site, s: *Shape, n: u32, to: *Stream, from: *Stream, also: u32, bytes: opt[Value]) res[Value, refusal.Error] {
    val res_to: res[Placed, refusal.Error] = partial(x, st, s, n, to, ?from.index);
    if (sel res_to.err) { ret res[Value, refusal.Error].err{res_to.err}; }
    val res_from: res[Placed, refusal.Error] = partial(x, st, s, n, from, ?to.index);
    if (sel res_from.err) { ret res[Value, refusal.Error].err{res_from.err}; }
    val err_ahead: err[refusal.Error] = ahead(x, st, s, n, deeper(x, deeper(x, res_to.ok.at, res_from.ok.at), also));
    if (sel err_ahead.err) { ret res[Value, refusal.Error].err{err_ahead.err}; }
    var length: Value = 0;
    if (sel bytes.some) { length = bytes.some; }
    or {
        val res_size: res[Value, refusal.Error] = emit.word_constant(st, s.word, to.size);
        if (sel res_size.err) { ret res_size; }
        length = emit.binary(st, table.MUL, trips(st, s), res_size.ok);
    }
    ret overlapping(st, s, res_to.ok.value, res_from.ok.value, length);
}

# how a stored stream lies against another stream of the loop, of the same element size, as far as is known before
# the loop runs
# ---
# apart:   in two distinct objects (`memory.apart`), so no element of one is an element of the other
# at:      the same base, at indices a constant apart: the bytes the stored one lies above the other on every trip, at
#          the stepping parameter's width
# unknown: anywhere, which only a test of their addresses where the loop is entered decides
tag Lie: u8 {
    apart;
    at: u64;
    unknown;
}

# the constant index `a` exceeds index `b` by on every trip, none where they differ by more than a constant
fun difference(a: *Affine, b: *Affine, bits: u32) opt[u64] {
    if (a.stride != b.stride || a.terms.len != b.terms.len) { ret opt[u64].none{}; }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < a.terms.len) {
        var found: bool  = false;
        var j:     usize = 0;
        for (j < b.terms.len) {
            if (b.terms.data[j].value == a.terms.data[k].value && b.terms.data[j].times == a.terms.data[k].times) { found = true; }
            j = j + 1;
        }
        if (!found) { ret opt[u64].none{}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret opt[u64].some{wrapped(a.constant - b.constant, bits)};
}

# how stream `to` lies against stream `from`
fun lie_of(x: *Run, s: *Shape, to: *Stream, from: *Stream) res[Lie, refusal.Error] {
    val bits: u32 = integer_bits(x, s.word);
    if (to.base == from.base) {
        val opt_apart: opt[u64] = difference(?to.index, ?from.index, bits);
        if (sel opt_apart.some) { ret res[Lie, refusal.Error].ok{Lie.at{wrapped(opt_apart.some * to.size, bits)}}; }
        ret res[Lie, refusal.Error].ok{Lie.unknown{}};
    }
    val res_apart: res[bool, refusal.Error] = memory.apart(x.mem, to.base, from.base);
    if (sel res_apart.err) { ret res[Lie, refusal.Error].err{res_apart.err}; }
    if (res_apart.ok)      { ret res[Lie, refusal.Error].ok{Lie.apart{}}; }
    ret res[Lie, refusal.Error].ok{Lie.unknown{}};
}

# whether a destination `apart` bytes above a source, at a width of `bits`, lies past it by between one byte and
# `bytes` less one, the case `overlapping` tests for, decided for numbers known before the loop runs
fun overlaps_at(apart: u64, bytes: u64, bits: u32) bool {
    ret wrapped(apart - 1, bits) < wrapped(bytes - 1, bits);
}

# the compare of the loop's own kind between `iv` and the bound, true where a trip runs
fun runs(st: *Site, s: *Shape, iv: Value) Value {
    if (s.left) { ret emit.binary(st, s.compare, iv, s.bound); }
    ret emit.binary(st, s.compare, s.bound, iv);
}

# the entry of the loop: a block in place of the edge from outside, which tests that a trip runs and branches to
# `taken`, passing it nothing, or to the header as before, passing `starts`, what the edge passed. the builder is
# left at the end of `taken`
fun entry(x: *Run, st: *Site, s: *Shape, taken: Block, starts: Slice[Value]) err[refusal.Error] {
    val gate: Block = builder.block(?st.bld, Slice[Declaration]{data: nil, size: 0});
    builder.at_end(?st.bld, gate);
    fork(st, runs(st, s, s.start), taken, no_values(), s.head, starts);
    val err_built: err[refusal.Error] = emit.done(st);
    if (sel err_built.err) { ret err_built; }
    val err_moved: err[refusal.Error] = edit(body.retarget(x.c.m, x.f, s.entering, s.edge, gate, no_values()));
    if (sel err_moved.err) { ret err_moved; }
    builder.at_end(?st.bld, taken);
    ret err[refusal.Error].ok{};
}

# the trips of a loop that runs at least one, as an unsigned count of the stepping parameter's width
fun trips(st: *Site, s: *Shape) Value {
    ret emit.binary(st, table.SUB, s.bound, s.start);
}

# the byte every byte of a constant of `bits` holds, none where they differ
fun equal_bytes(x: u64, bits: u32) opt[u64] {
    if (bits == 0 || bits > 64 || bits % 8 != 0) { ret opt[u64].none{}; }
    val low: u64 = x & 0xff;
    var k:   u32 = 8;
    for (k < bits) {
        if (((x >> k::u64) & 0xff) != low) { ret opt[u64].none{}; }
        k = k + 8;
    }
    ret opt[u64].some{low};
}

# the bits a store of an integer or float type writes, its width or its format's, zero for any other type
fun encoded_bits(x: *Run, ty: Type) u32 {
    val res_shape: res[type_table.Shape, type_table.Error] = type_table.shape(?x.c.m.types, ty);
    if (sel res_shape.err)         { ret 0; }
    if (sel res_shape.ok.integer)  { ret res_shape.ok.integer.width; }
    if (!(sel res_shape.ok.float)) { ret 0; }
    val opt_row: opt[FormatRow] = format_row(res_shape.ok.float.format);
    if (sel opt_row.none) { ret 0; }
    ret opt_row.some.width;
}

# the byte a fill of value `v` stores, a value the builder may read, none where its bytes differ. a constant integer
# or float qualifies when its encoding covers every byte of its type's size and those bytes are one byte, since its
# store then writes that byte to each byte of the element, whatever the byte order
fun fill_byte(x: *Run, st: *Site, v: Value) res[opt[Value], refusal.Error] {
    val b: *Body = body_of(x);
    if (integer_bits(x, b.values.data[v].type) == 8) { ret res[opt[Value], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Value].some{v}}; }
    val opt_known: opt[u64] = emit.encoding_in(x.c.m, b, v);
    if (sel opt_known.none) { ret res[opt[Value], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Value].none{}}; }
    val res_size: res[u64, TargetError] = layout.size(?x.layout, b.values.data[v].type, type_table.DEFAULT_SPACE);
    if (sel res_size.err)                                               { ret res[opt[Value], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Value].none{}}; }
    if (encoded_bits(x, b.values.data[v].type)::u64 != res_size.ok * 8) { ret res[opt[Value], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Value].none{}}; }
    val opt_byte: opt[u64] = equal_bytes(opt_known.some, (res_size.ok * 8)::u32);
    if (sel opt_byte.none) { ret res[opt[Value], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Value].none{}}; }
    val res_byte_type: res[Type, refusal.Error] = integer_type(x, 8);
    if (sel res_byte_type.err) { ret res[opt[Value], refusal.Error].err{res_byte_type.err}; }
    val res_made: res[Value, refusal.Error] = emit.constant(st, res_byte_type.ok, word.small(opt_byte.some));
    if (sel res_made.err) { ret res[opt[Value], refusal.Error].err{res_made.err}; }
    ret res[opt[Value], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Value].some{res_made.ok}};
}

# the destination lies past the source by between one byte and `bytes` less one, where an element loop that reads
# each element before it writes the same one differs from the operation over the whole run: true where it does.
# `to` and `from` are the two streams' origins, which lie as far apart as their elements at any one trip
fun overlapping(st: *Site, s: *Shape, to: Value, from: Value, bytes: Value) res[Value, refusal.Error] {
    var imm:     [1]Immediate              = [1]Immediate{Immediate.ty{s.word}};
    var ops_t:   [1]Value                  = [1]Value{to};
    var ops_f:   [1]Value                  = [1]Value{from};
    val at_to:   Value                     = builder.value(?st.bld, Request{opcode: table.PTRTOINT, operands: Slice[Value]{data: ?ops_t[0], size: 1}, immediates: Slice[Immediate]{data: ?imm[0], size: 1}, targets: Slice[Branch]{data: nil, size: 0}});
    val at_from: Value                     = builder.value(?st.bld, Request{opcode: table.PTRTOINT, operands: Slice[Value]{data: ?ops_f[0], size: 1}, immediates: Slice[Immediate]{data: ?imm[0], size: 1}, targets: Slice[Branch]{data: nil, size: 0}});
    val res_one: res[Value, refusal.Error] = emit.word_constant(st, s.word, 1);
    if (sel res_one.err) { ret res_one; }
    val apart: Value = emit.binary(st, table.SUB, at_to, at_from);
    ret res[Value, refusal.Error].ok{emit.binary(st, table.LT_U, emit.binary(st, table.SUB, apart, res_one.ok), emit.binary(st, table.SUB, bytes, res_one.ok))};
}

# the flags of a copy that may run upward
fun ascending() Flags {
    var f: Flags = NO_FLAGS;
    f.ascending = true;
    ret f;
}

# take a copy or fill loop: the copy or fill of its whole run stands for it where a trip runs and, for a copy, the
# arrays do not overlap the way that would tell them apart. a copy whose arrays are apart, or whose destination lies
# at or below its source by a constant, needs no test, since an upward copy then gives what the loop gave. the copy
# or fill states the memory as the loop's store did: secret where it was marked so, and public where its store and a
# copy's load were and none of its operands is secret, its length being the trip count made a value. answers whether
# it took the loop
fun bulk(x: *Run, n: u32, s: *Shape, acc: *Accesses) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    if (acc.stores.len != 1 || acc.loads.len > 1 || acc.ops.len != 0) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    val b:   *Body   = body_of(x);
    val out: *Access = ?acc.stores.data[0];
    if (b.blocks.data[s.head].parameters.len != 1) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    if (!pointer_wide(x, s, out.stream.base))      { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    var copy: bool = false;
    var test: bool = false;
    if (acc.loads.len == 1) {
        val inp: *Access = ?acc.loads.data[0];
        if (inp.value != out.value || inp.stream.size != out.stream.size) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        if (!pointer_wide(x, s, inp.stream.base))                         { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        copy = true;
        val res_lie: res[Lie, refusal.Error] = lie_of(x, s, ?out.stream, ?inp.stream);
        if (sel res_lie.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_lie.err}; }
        test = sel res_lie.ok.unknown;
        if (sel res_lie.ok.at) {
            val bits: u32 = integer_bits(x, s.word);
            test = res_lie.ok.at != 0 && ((res_lie.ok.at >> (bits - 1)::u64) & 1) == 0;
        }
    }
    or (!outside(x, n, out.value)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }

    var st: Site = emit.init(x.c.m, x.f, b, x.a);
    fin { emit.dnit(?st); }
    var opt_byte: opt[Value] = opt[Value].none{};
    if (!copy) {
        val res_byte: res[opt[Value], refusal.Error] = fill_byte(x, ?st, out.value);
        if (sel res_byte.err)     { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_byte.err}; }
        if (sel res_byte.ok.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        opt_byte = res_byte.ok;
    }
    val res_size: res[Value, refusal.Error] = emit.word_constant(?st, s.word, out.stream.size);
    if (sel res_size.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_size.err}; }

    # the origins, and the test where the arrays' places do not settle it, ahead of the loops whose entries fix them
    val err_out: err[refusal.Error] = adjust(x, ?st, s, n, ?out.stream);
    if (sel err_out.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{err_out.err}; }
    var over: Value = 0;
    if (copy) {
        val inp:    *Access            = ?acc.loads.data[0];
        val err_in: err[refusal.Error] = adjust(x, ?st, s, n, ?inp.stream);
        if (sel err_in.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{err_in.err}; }
        if (test) {
            var run:      [2]Value                  = [2]Value{s.start, s.bound};
            val res_over: res[Value, refusal.Error] = tested(x, ?st, s, n, ?out.stream, ?inp.stream, placement(x, n, Slice[Value]{data: ?run[0], size: 2}), opt[Value].none{});
            if (sel res_over.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_over.err}; }
            over = res_over.ok;
        }
    }

    var start:     [1]Value           = [1]Value{s.start};
    val taken:     Block              = builder.block(?st.bld, Slice[Declaration]{data: nil, size: 0});
    val err_entry: err[refusal.Error] = entry(x, ?st, s, taken, Slice[Value]{data: ?start[0], size: 1});
    if (sel err_entry.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{err_entry.err}; }
    val bytes: Value    = emit.binary(?st, table.MUL, trips(?st, s), res_size.ok);
    val to:    Value    = element(?st, out.stream, s.start);
    var end:   [1]Value = [1]Value{s.bound};
    if (copy) {
        val inp:  *Access = ?acc.loads.data[0];
        val from: Value   = element(?st, inp.stream, s.start);
        if (test) {
            val whole: Block = builder.block(?st.bld, Slice[Declaration]{data: nil, size: 0});
            fork(?st, over, s.head, Slice[Value]{data: ?start[0], size: 1}, whole, no_values());
            builder.at_end(?st.bld, whole);
        }
        var ops:   [3]Value = [3]Value{to, from, bytes};
        var align: u64      = out.stream.align;
        if (inp.stream.align < align) { align = inp.stream.align; }
        var imm:   [1]Immediate = [1]Immediate{Immediate.alignment{align}};
        var flags: Flags        = ascending();
        flags.public = b.instructions.data[out.at].metadata.flags.public && b.instructions.data[inp.at].metadata.flags.public && public_all(b, Slice[Value]{data: ?ops[0], size: 3});
        builder.flags(?st.bld, flags);
        builder.secret(?st.bld, b.instructions.data[out.at].metadata.secret);
        builder.emit(?st.bld, Request{opcode: table.MEM_COPY, operands: Slice[Value]{data: ?ops[0], size: 3}, immediates: Slice[Immediate]{data: ?imm[0], size: 1}, targets: Slice[Branch]{data: nil, size: 0}});
        builder.flags(?st.bld, NO_FLAGS);
        builder.secret(?st.bld, false);
    }
    or (sel opt_byte.some) {
        var ops:   [3]Value     = [3]Value{to, opt_byte.some, bytes};
        var imm:   [1]Immediate = [1]Immediate{Immediate.alignment{out.stream.align}};
        var flags: Flags        = NO_FLAGS;
        flags.public = b.instructions.data[out.at].metadata.flags.public && public_all(b, Slice[Value]{data: ?ops[0], size: 3});
        builder.flags(?st.bld, flags);
        builder.secret(?st.bld, b.instructions.data[out.at].metadata.secret);
        builder.emit(?st.bld, Request{opcode: table.MEM_FILL, operands: Slice[Value]{data: ?ops[0], size: 3}, immediates: Slice[Immediate]{data: ?imm[0], size: 1}, targets: Slice[Branch]{data: nil, size: 0}});
        builder.flags(?st.bld, NO_FLAGS);
        builder.secret(?st.bld, false);
    }
    jump(?st, s.head, Slice[Value]{data: ?end[0], size: 1});
    val err_built: err[refusal.Error] = emit.done(?st);
    if (sel err_built.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{err_built.err}; }
    ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{true};
}

# whether no value of a list is secret, as no operand of an access stated public is
fun public_all(b: *Body, vs: Slice[Value]) bool {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < vs.size) {
        if (b.values.data[vs.data[k]].secret) { ret false; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret true;
}

# the most lanes the pass asks a unit for
val MOST: u32 = 64;

# what the pass made of each scalar value of the latch it carries out on vectors
# ---
# from: the scalar values
# to:   the vector each stands as, in the same order
rec Made {
    from: vector.Vector[Value];
    to:   vector.Vector[Value];
}

# the vector a scalar value stands as, none where none was made
fun made_of(m: *Made, v: Value) opt[Value] {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < m.from.len) {
        if (m.from.data[k] == v) { ret opt[Value].some{m.to.data[k]}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret opt[Value].none{};
}

fun note(m: *Made, from: Value, to: Value) err[refusal.Error] {
    val res_from: res[usize, allocator.Error] = vector.push[Value](?m.from, from);
    if (sel res_from.err) { ret err[refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_from.err}}; }
    val res_to: res[usize, allocator.Error] = vector.push[Value](?m.to, to);
    if (sel res_to.err) { ret err[refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_to.err}}; }
    ret err[refusal.Error].ok{};
}

# whether a value is a load's result of the latch
fun loaded(acc: *Accesses, v: Value) bool {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < acc.loads.len) {
        if (acc.loads.data[k].value == v) { ret true; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether a scalar the vector loop reads as it stands is one it can give: a load's result, whose vector it loads, or
# a value the loop does not define, which a splat gives every lane
fun valid(x: *Run, n: u32, acc: *Accesses, v: Value) bool {
    ret loaded(acc, v) || outside(x, n, v);
}

# the lane type of the target's declarations a scalar type is, a float's format written to `format`
fun lane_of(x: *Run, ty: Type, format: *Format) opt[LaneType] {
    val res_shape: res[type_table.Shape, type_table.Error] = type_table.shape(?x.c.m.types, ty);
    if (sel res_shape.err)        { ret opt[LaneType].none{}; }
    if (sel res_shape.ok.integer) { ret opt[LaneType].some{LaneType.integer{res_shape.ok.integer.width}}; }
    if (sel res_shape.ok.float) {
        @format = res_shape.ok.float.format;
        ret opt[LaneType].some{LaneType.float{format}};
    }
    ret opt[LaneType].none{};
}

# the bits one lane of a scalar type takes, zero for a type no lane is
fun lane_bits(x: *Run, ty: Type) u32 {
    var format:   Format;
    val opt_lane: opt[LaneType] = lane_of(x, ty, ?format);
    if (sel opt_lane.none) { ret 0; }
    ret units.bits_of(opt_lane.some);
}

# the integer type of a width
fun integer_type(x: *Run, bits: u32) res[Type, refusal.Error] {
    val res_made: res[Type, type_table.Error] = type_table.intern(?x.c.m.types, type_table.Shape.integer{type_table.Integer{width: bits}});
    if (sel res_made.err) { ret res[Type, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.ir{module.Error.types{res_made.err}}}; }
    ret res[Type, refusal.Error].ok{res_made.ok};
}

# how the function requires constant time
fun time_of(x: *Run) ConstantTime {
    ret x.c.m.functions.data[x.f].data.constant_time;
}

fun unread() refusal.Error {
    ret refusal.Error.reason{"the target's vector units could not be read"};
}

# the lanes of each piece the function's code splits a vector of `c` lanes of a scalar type into, as every
# legalisation splits it for the function (`mirl.target.vector.split_for`), zero where it takes them lane by lane
fun piece_of(x: *Run, ty: Type, c: u32) res[u32, refusal.Error] {
    var format:   Format;
    val opt_lane: opt[LaneType] = lane_of(x, ty, ?format);
    if (sel opt_lane.none) { ret res[u32, refusal.Error].ok{0}; }
    val res_split: res[Split, units.Error] = units.split_for(x.c.basis, time_of(x), ?x.c.t.caps, opt_lane.some, c);
    if (sel res_split.err)          { ret res[u32, refusal.Error].err{unread()}; }
    if (!(sel res_split.ok.pieces)) { ret res[u32, refusal.Error].ok{0}; }
    ret res[u32, refusal.Error].ok{res_split.ok.pieces.lanes};
}

# whether a unit the function's code meets computes an operation over `count` packed lanes, holding that many lanes
# of every lane type it reads and gives (`mirl.target.vector.packed` and `holds_for`): the question the vector
# legalisation asks of each run it packs, and with `direct` also that the unit's row is not expanded
# (`mirl.target.vector.direct`), the question of a step the vectoriser forms
# ---
# code:   the operation
# lane:   the lane type it reads
# to:     the lane type it gives, lane for any but a conversion
# types:  every lane type it reads and gives, at most four
# count:  the lanes of the run
# direct: whether an expanded row is refused
fun packed_any(x: *Run, code: Opcode, lane: Type, to: Type, types: Slice[Type], count: u32, direct: bool) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    val v: capability.Vectors = x.c.t.caps.vectors;
    if (!(sel v.units)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    if (types.size > 4) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    var fa:       Format;
    var fb:       Format;
    val opt_lane: opt[LaneType] = lane_of(x, lane, ?fa);
    val opt_to:   opt[LaneType] = lane_of(x, to, ?fb);
    if (sel opt_lane.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    if (sel opt_to.none)   { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    var fs: [4]Format;
    var ls: [4]LaneType;
    var k:  usize = 0;
    for (k < types.size) {
        val opt_each: opt[LaneType] = lane_of(x, types.data[k], ?fs[k]);
        if (sel opt_each.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        ls[k] = opt_each.some;
        k     = k + 1;
    }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < v.units.size) {
        val u:          *capability.Unit       = ?v.units.data[i];
        val res_packed: res[bool, units.Error] = asked(x, u, code, opt_lane.some, opt_to.some, direct);
        if (sel res_packed.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{unread()}; }
        var all: bool = res_packed.ok;
        k = 0;
        for (all && k < types.size) {
            val res_holds: res[bool, units.Error] = units.holds_for(x.c.basis, time_of(x), u, ls[k], count);
            if (sel res_holds.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{unread()}; }
            all = res_holds.ok;
            k   = k + 1;
        }
        if (all) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{true}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false};
}

# whether a unit packs an operation for the function, and with `direct` by a row that is not expanded
fun asked(x: *Run, u: *capability.Unit, code: Opcode, lane: LaneType, to: LaneType, direct: bool) res[bool, units.Error] {
    if (direct) { ret units.direct(x.c.basis, time_of(x), u, code, lane, to); }
    ret units.packed(x.c.basis, time_of(x), u, code, lane, to);
}

# whether a unit the function's code meets that widens its masks computes a comparison of `count` lanes and the sign
# extension of its mask to integer lanes as wide as those compared as one operation: a row states the comparison, not
# expanded, and the unit holds that many lanes of both types, the vector legalisation's question of a comparison read
# only by that extension with the vectoriser's of a step it forms
fun fused_any(x: *Run, code: Opcode, lane: Type, wide: Type, count: u32) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    val v: capability.Vectors = x.c.t.caps.vectors;
    if (!(sel v.units)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    var fa:       Format;
    var fb:       Format;
    val opt_lane: opt[LaneType] = lane_of(x, lane, ?fa);
    val opt_wide: opt[LaneType] = lane_of(x, wide, ?fb);
    if (sel opt_lane.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    if (sel opt_wide.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < v.units.size) {
        val u: *capability.Unit = ?v.units.data[i];
        if (sel u.masks.widened) {
            val res_packed: res[bool, units.Error] = units.direct(x.c.basis, time_of(x), u, code, opt_lane.some, opt_lane.some);
            if (sel res_packed.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{unread()}; }
            val res_lane: res[bool, units.Error] = units.holds_for(x.c.basis, time_of(x), u, opt_lane.some, count);
            if (sel res_lane.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{unread()}; }
            val res_wide: res[bool, units.Error] = units.holds_for(x.c.basis, time_of(x), u, opt_wide.some, count);
            if (sel res_wide.err)                            { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{unread()}; }
            if (res_packed.ok && res_lane.ok && res_wide.ok) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{true}; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false};
}

# whether a run of `run` lanes of a lane type is cut packed from a piece of `piece` lanes: a shuffle at both counts,
# as the vector legalisation cuts an operand's run from the piece holding it
fun cut(x: *Run, ty: Type, piece: u32, run: u32) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    var one:      [1]Type                  = [1]Type{ty};
    val res_from: res[bool, refusal.Error] = packed_any(x, table.VSHUFFLE, ty, ty, Slice[Type]{data: ?one[0], size: 1}, piece, false);
    if (sel res_from.err) { ret res_from; }
    if (!res_from.ok)     { ret res_from; }
    ret packed_any(x, table.VSHUFFLE, ty, ty, Slice[Type]{data: ?one[0], size: 1}, run, false);
}

# whether the function's code computes a step of the vector loop packed, as the vector legalisation takes it at `c`
# lanes: over the runs of its widest lane type, each run a whole piece of its result, each operand's run cut from the
# piece holding it by a packed shuffle where that piece is wider, and a unit computing the operation over the run by
# a row that is not expanded
# ---
# code:     the operation
# lane:     the lane type it reads
# to:       the lane type it gives, lane for any but a conversion
# operands: the lane types of its operands, at most three
# result:   the lane type of its result
fun served_step(x: *Run, code: Opcode, lane: Type, to: Type, operands: Slice[Type], result: Type, c: u32) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    if (operands.size > 3) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    var all:    [4]Type;
    var widest: Type  = result;
    var k:      usize = 0;
    for (k < operands.size) {
        all[k] = operands.data[k];
        if (lane_bits(x, operands.data[k]) > lane_bits(x, widest)) { widest = operands.data[k]; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    all[operands.size] = result;
    val res_run: res[u32, refusal.Error] = piece_of(x, widest, c);
    if (sel res_run.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_run.err}; }
    val run: u32 = res_run.ok;
    if (run == 0) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    val res_out: res[u32, refusal.Error] = piece_of(x, result, c);
    if (sel res_out.err)   { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_out.err}; }
    if (res_out.ok != run) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    k = 0;
    for (k < operands.size) {
        val res_piece: res[u32, refusal.Error] = piece_of(x, operands.data[k], c);
        if (sel res_piece.err)  { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_piece.err}; }
        if (res_piece.ok < run) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        if (res_piece.ok > run) {
            val res_cut: res[bool, refusal.Error] = cut(x, operands.data[k], res_piece.ok, run);
            if (sel res_cut.err) { ret res_cut; }
            if (!res_cut.ok)     { ret res_cut; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret packed_any(x, code, lane, to, Slice[Type]{data: ?all[0], size: operands.size + 1}, run, true);
}

# whether the function's code computes a comparison of `c` lanes of `compared` and the sign extension of its mask to
# `wide`, integer lanes as wide, packed: as one operation where a unit widens its masks (`fused_any`), and otherwise
# the comparison giving a vector of conditions and its extension, each a step `served_step` answers
fun compare_served(x: *Run, code: Opcode, compared: Type, wide: Type, condition: Type, c: u32) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    val res_run: res[u32, refusal.Error] = piece_of(x, compared, c);
    if (sel res_run.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_run.err}; }
    if (res_run.ok == 0) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    val res_fused: res[bool, refusal.Error] = fused_any(x, code, compared, wide, res_run.ok);
    if (sel res_fused.err) { ret res_fused; }
    if (res_fused.ok)      { ret res_fused; }
    var pair:    [2]Type                  = [2]Type{compared, compared};
    val res_cmp: res[bool, refusal.Error] = served_step(x, code, compared, compared, Slice[Type]{data: ?pair[0], size: 2}, condition, c);
    if (sel res_cmp.err) { ret res_cmp; }
    if (!res_cmp.ok)     { ret res_cmp; }
    var one: [1]Type = [1]Type{condition};
    ret served_step(x, table.EXT_S, condition, wide, Slice[Type]{data: ?one[0], size: 1}, wide, c);
}

# whether the function's code computes an operation of one lane type, a splat or a reduction, over the runs of `c`
# lanes of it packed
fun served_whole(x: *Run, code: Opcode, ty: Type, c: u32) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    val res_run: res[u32, refusal.Error] = piece_of(x, ty, c);
    if (sel res_run.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_run.err}; }
    if (res_run.ok == 0) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    var one: [1]Type = [1]Type{ty};
    ret packed_any(x, code, ty, ty, Slice[Type]{data: ?one[0], size: 1}, res_run.ok, false);
}

# whether an operation converts each lane exactly: a zero or sign extension, or an integer's conversion to a float
fun conversion(op: Opcode) bool {
    ret op == table.EXT_U || op == table.EXT_S || op == table.ITOF_U || op == table.ITOF_S;
}

# whether an operation compares two values lane by lane, giving a condition of each lane
fun comparison(op: Opcode) bool {
    ret (op >= table.EQ && op <= table.GE_U) || op == table.FLT_O || (op >= table.FEQ_O && op <= table.FUNO);
}

# the extension of the kind a conversion reads its operand as: zero for an unsigned one, sign for a signed one
fun extension_of(code: Opcode) Opcode {
    if (code == table.EXT_U || code == table.ITOF_U) { ret table.EXT_U; }
    ret table.EXT_S;
}

# how a conversion is formed
# ---
# width: the bits of the integer it goes through, zero where the conversion is formed itself
# last:  the conversion from that integer
rec Via {
    width: u32;
    last:  Opcode;
}

# how a conversion `code` from `from` to `to` is formed at `c` lanes, none where no way is computed packed: by itself,
# or through a wider integer, the extension of the kind the conversion reads (`extension_of`), itself formed the same
# way, and then the conversion from that integer. an extension of an extension of one kind is that extension, and a
# float conversion of an integer's value-keeping extension gives what the conversion of the integer gives, since its
# result depends on the value alone. an extension goes through a width below `to`'s, a float conversion through one
# up to 64 bits, the widest first, and an unsigned float conversion through the signed one first, exact since a zero
# extension to a wider integer is never negative
fun route(x: *Run, code: Opcode, from: Type, to: Type, c: u32, depth: u32) res[opt[Via], refusal.Error] {
    var one:        [1]Type                  = [1]Type{from};
    val res_direct: res[bool, refusal.Error] = served_step(x, code, from, to, Slice[Type]{data: ?one[0], size: 1}, to, c);
    if (sel res_direct.err) { ret res[opt[Via], refusal.Error].err{res_direct.err}; }
    if (res_direct.ok)      { ret res[opt[Via], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Via].some{Via{width: 0, last: code}}}; }
    val bits: u32 = integer_bits(x, from);
    if (depth > 3 || bits == 0) { ret res[opt[Via], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Via].none{}}; }
    var top: u32 = 64;
    if (code == table.EXT_U || code == table.EXT_S) { top = integer_bits(x, to) - 1; }
    var m: u32 = 64;
    for (m > bits) {
        if (m <= top) {
            val res_mid: res[Type, refusal.Error] = integer_type(x, m);
            if (sel res_mid.err) { ret res[opt[Via], refusal.Error].err{res_mid.err}; }
            val res_via: res[opt[Via], refusal.Error] = route(x, extension_of(code), from, res_mid.ok, c, depth + 1);
            if (sel res_via.err) { ret res_via; }
            if (sel res_via.ok.some) {
                var mid: [1]Type = [1]Type{res_mid.ok};
                var k:   u32     = 0;
                for (k < 2) {
                    var last: Opcode = code;
                    if (k == 0 && code == table.ITOF_U) { last = table.ITOF_S; }
                    val res_last: res[bool, refusal.Error] = served_step(x, last, res_mid.ok, to, Slice[Type]{data: ?mid[0], size: 1}, to, c);
                    if (sel res_last.err) { ret res[opt[Via], refusal.Error].err{res_last.err}; }
                    if (res_last.ok)      { ret res[opt[Via], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Via].some{Via{width: m, last: last}}}; }
                    k = k + 1;
                }
            }
        }
        m = m / 2;
    }
    ret res[opt[Via], refusal.Error].ok{opt[Via].none{}};
}

# an operand of a step of the vector loop
# ---
# value: a scalar of the loop, a load's result or an accumulator, whose vector the loop makes, or a value the loop
#        does not define, splat to every lane ahead of it
# step:  the result of an earlier step, by its position
tag Source: u8 {
    value: Value;
    step:  u32;
}

# one operation of the vector loop, over vectors of the loop's lane count
# ---
# code:   the operation
# first:  its first operand
# second: its second, where it reads two
# count:  how many operands it reads
# lane:   the scalar type of its result's lanes
# origin: the instruction of the latch it reads as
rec Step {
    code:   Opcode;
    first:  Source;
    second: Source;
    count:  u32;
    lane:   Type;
    origin: Instruction;
}

# the steps of the vector loop in order, and the scalar value of the latch each stands for
# ---
# steps: the steps
# from:  the values of the latch a step stands for
# to:    the step each stands for, in the same order
rec Plan {
    steps: vector.Vector[Step];
    from:  vector.Vector[Value];
    to:    vector.Vector[u32];
}

# add a step to the plan, answering its position (`vector.push` answers the new length)
fun push_step(p: *Plan, s: Step) res[u32, refusal.Error] {
    val res_pushed: res[usize, allocator.Error] = vector.push[Step](?p.steps, s);
    if (sel res_pushed.err) { ret res[u32, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_pushed.err}}; }
    ret res[u32, refusal.Error].ok{(res_pushed.ok - 1)::u32};
}

fun stand(p: *Plan, v: Value, k: u32) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    val res_from: res[usize, allocator.Error] = vector.push[Value](?p.from, v);
    if (sel res_from.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_from.err}}; }
    val res_to: res[usize, allocator.Error] = vector.push[u32](?p.to, k);
    if (sel res_to.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_to.err}}; }
    ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{true};
}

# what the vector loop reads for a scalar of the latch: the step standing for it, or the value itself
fun source_of(p: *Plan, v: Value) Source {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < p.from.len) {
        if (p.from.data[k] == v) { ret Source.step{p.to.data[k]}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret Source.value{v};
}

# the scalar type of a source's lanes
fun source_type(x: *Run, p: *Plan, s: Source) Type {
    if (sel s.step) { ret p.steps.data[s.step].lane; }
    ret body_of(x).values.data[s.value].type;
}

# the steps that form conversion `code` of `s` from `from` to `to` (`route`), answering the last, none where no way
# is computed packed
fun widen(x: *Run, p: *Plan, code: Opcode, s: Source, from: Type, to: Type, c: u32, origin: Instruction) res[opt[u32], refusal.Error] {
    val res_via: res[opt[Via], refusal.Error] = route(x, code, from, to, c, 0);
    if (sel res_via.err)     { ret res[opt[u32], refusal.Error].err{res_via.err}; }
    if (sel res_via.ok.none) { ret res[opt[u32], refusal.Error].ok{opt[u32].none{}}; }
    var at: Source = s;
    if (res_via.ok.some.width != 0) {
        val res_mid: res[Type, refusal.Error] = integer_type(x, res_via.ok.some.width);
        if (sel res_mid.err) { ret res[opt[u32], refusal.Error].err{res_mid.err}; }
        val res_inner: res[opt[u32], refusal.Error] = widen(x, p, extension_of(code), s, from, res_mid.ok, c, origin);
        if (sel res_inner.err)     { ret res_inner; }
        if (sel res_inner.ok.none) { ret res_inner; }
        at = Source.step{res_inner.ok.some};
    }
    val res_k: res[u32, refusal.Error] = push_step(p, Step{code: res_via.ok.some.last, first: at, second: at, count: 1, lane: to, origin: origin});
    if (sel res_k.err) { ret res[opt[u32], refusal.Error].err{res_k.err}; }
    ret res[opt[u32], refusal.Error].ok{opt[u32].some{res_k.ok}};
}

# an accumulator of the loop: a header parameter each trip combines one value into by an operation the pass may
# regroup, or, where a select chooses the parameter's next value, combines a value into only where a condition holds
# ---
# index:  its position among the header's parameters
# param:  the parameter
# op:     the operation of the latch that combines a value into it
# reduce: the reduction of a vector's lanes by that operation
# start:  what the edge from outside passes it
# result: what the branch back passes it: the operation's result, or the select's
# choice: the select between the operation's result and the parameter, NO_INSTRUCTION where there is none
# taken:  the select takes the operation's result where its condition holds
# other:  the value the operation combines into it
rec Accumulator {
    index:  u32;
    param:  Value;
    op:     Instruction;
    reduce: Opcode;
    start:  Value;
    result: Value;
    choice: Instruction;
    taken:  bool;
    other:  Value;
}

# the reduction of a vector's lanes by an operation an accumulator may combine with: integer sums, products and the
# three bitwise operations, which regroup exactly, and float sums and products where the build permits float
# reassociation (`mirl.pass.relaxation.FLOAT_REASSOC`), none for any other
fun reducing(x: *Run, code: Opcode) opt[Opcode] {
    if (code == table.ADD)                                       { ret opt[Opcode].some{table.REDUCE_ADD}; }
    if (code == table.MUL)                                       { ret opt[Opcode].some{table.REDUCE_MUL}; }
    if (code == table.AND)                                       { ret opt[Opcode].some{table.REDUCE_AND}; }
    if (code == table.OR)                                        { ret opt[Opcode].some{table.REDUCE_OR}; }
    if (code == table.XOR)                                       { ret opt[Opcode].some{table.REDUCE_XOR}; }
    if (!relaxation.holds(x.c.floats, relaxation.FLOAT_REASSOC)) { ret opt[Opcode].none{}; }
    if (code == table.FADD)                                      { ret opt[Opcode].some{table.REDUCE_FADD_ANY}; }
    if (code == table.FMUL)                                      { ret opt[Opcode].some{table.REDUCE_FMUL_ANY}; }
    ret opt[Opcode].none{};
}

# whether instruction `i` is one of the latch's operations the vector loop carries
fun in_ops(acc: *Accesses, i: Instruction) bool {
    var j: usize = 0;
    for (j < acc.ops.len) {
        if (acc.ops.data[j] == i) { ret true; }
        j = j + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# the instruction of the latch whose one result a value is, none for any other value
fun op_of(x: *Run, acc: *Accesses, v: Value) opt[Instruction] {
    val def: Def = body_of(x).values.data[v].def;
    if (!(sel def.result))                    { ret opt[Instruction].none{}; }
    if (!in_ops(acc, def.result.instruction)) { ret opt[Instruction].none{}; }
    ret opt[Instruction].some{def.result.instruction};
}

# the accumulators of the loop onto `into`: every header parameter but the index, false where one is not an
# accumulator. its latch reads it in an operation of the latch's that combines it with one other value and that
# `reducing` takes, and the branch back passes the operation's result, read by nothing else; or the branch back passes
# a select, read by nothing else, of the parameter and that operation's result, read by nothing but the select, by a
# comparison of the latch, the operation an integer sum, or or exclusive or, whose identity zero leaves a value as it
# is, and the parameter read by nothing else of the latch
fun accumulators(x: *Run, s: *Shape, acc: *Accesses, into: *vector.Vector[Accumulator]) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    val b:      *Body       = body_of(x);
    val last:   Instruction = b.blocks.data[s.latch].last;
    val params: usize       = b.blocks.data[s.head].parameters.len;
    if (b.instructions.data[last].edges.len != 1 || b.instructions.data[last].edges.data[0].block != s.head) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < params) {
        if (k != s.iv::usize) {
            val p:      Value            = b.blocks.data[s.head].parameters.data[k];
            val r:      Value            = b.instructions.data[last].edges.data[0].arguments.data[k];
            val opt_op: opt[Instruction] = op_of(x, acc, r);
            if (sel opt_op.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            var op:     Instruction      = opt_op.some;
            var choice: Instruction      = NO_INSTRUCTION;
            var taken:  bool             = true;
            val dr:     *InstructionData = ?b.instructions.data[op];
            if (dr.opcode == table.SELECT) {
                if (dr.operands.len != 3) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
                var q: Value = dr.operands.data[1];
                if (dr.operands.data[1] == p) {
                    q     = dr.operands.data[2];
                    taken = false;
                }
                or (dr.operands.data[2] != p) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
                if (q == p)                   { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
                val opt_cond: opt[Instruction] = op_of(x, acc, dr.operands.data[0]);
                if (sel opt_cond.none)                                      { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
                if (!comparison(b.instructions.data[opt_cond.some].opcode)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
                val opt_q: opt[Instruction] = op_of(x, acc, q);
                if (sel opt_q.none)                              { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
                if (b.values.data[q].uses.len != 1)              { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
                if (integer_bits(x, b.values.data[p].type) == 0) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
                val code: Opcode = b.instructions.data[opt_q.some].opcode;
                if (code != table.ADD && code != table.OR && code != table.XOR) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
                choice = op;
                op     = opt_q.some;
            }
            val d:          *InstructionData = ?b.instructions.data[op];
            val opt_reduce: opt[Opcode]      = reducing(x, d.opcode);
            if (sel opt_reduce.none)                                    { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            if (d.operands.len != 2)                                    { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            if ((d.operands.data[0] == p) == (d.operands.data[1] == p)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            var other: Value = d.operands.data[0];
            if (other == p) { other = d.operands.data[1]; }
            val rv: *ValueData = ?b.values.data[r];
            if (rv.uses.len != 1 || rv.uses.data[0].instruction != last) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            val pv: *ValueData = ?b.values.data[p];
            var u:  usize      = 0;
            for (u < pv.uses.len) {
                val user:  Instruction = pv.uses.data[u].instruction;
                val place: Place       = b.instructions.data[user].place;
                if (sel place.placed && place.placed == s.latch && user != op && user != choice) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
                u = u + 1;
            }
            val start:      Value                       = b.instructions.data[s.entering].edges.data[s.edge].arguments.data[k];
            val res_pushed: res[usize, allocator.Error] = vector.push[Accumulator](into, Accumulator{index: k::u32, param: p, op: op, reduce: opt_reduce.some, start: start, result: r, choice: choice, taken: taken, other: other});
            if (sel res_pushed.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_pushed.err}}; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{true};
}

# the vector every lane of which an accumulator's operation leaves a value as it is: zero for a sum, an or and an
# exclusive or, one for a product, every bit for an and, and for floats the format's negative zero for a sum (a
# positive zero would turn a sum of negative zeros positive) and one for a product
fun identity(x: *Run, st: *Site, code: Opcode, lane: Type, vec: Type) res[Value, refusal.Error] {
    val res_shape: res[type_table.Shape, type_table.Error] = type_table.shape(?x.c.m.types, lane);
    if (sel res_shape.err) { ret res[Value, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.ir{module.Error.types{res_shape.err}}}; }
    if (sel res_shape.ok.integer) {
        val bits: u32 = res_shape.ok.integer.width;
        var all:  u64 = ~(0::u64);
        if (bits < 64) { all = (1::u64 << bits::u64) - 1; }
        var k: u64 = 0;
        if (code == table.MUL) { k = 1; }
        if (code == table.AND) { k = all; }
        ret emit.constant(st, vec, word.small(k));
    }
    if (sel res_shape.ok.float) {
        val opt_row: opt[FormatRow] = format_row(res_shape.ok.float.format);
        if (sel opt_row.none) { ret res[Value, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.reason{"a float accumulator of a format with no row"}}; }
        val row: FormatRow = opt_row.some;
        if (sel row.encoding.binary) {
            val bin: Binary = row.encoding.binary;
            if (row.width <= 64) {
                var k: u64 = 1::u64 << (row.width - 1)::u64;
                if (code == table.FMUL) { k = bin.bias::u64 << bin.significand::u64; }
                ret emit.float_constant(st, vec, word.small(k));
            }
        }
        ret res[Value, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.reason{"a float accumulator of a format the vectoriser states no identity of"}};
    }
    ret res[Value, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.reason{"an accumulator of a type that is no integer or float"}};
}

# the step of `value` where a mask's lane holds, zero where it does not, onto `p`: `and(value, keep)`, or
# `and(value, not(keep))` where the value is taken where the mask does not hold, each lane of `ty`. none where the
# function's code does not compute them packed
fun masked(x: *Run, c: u32, p: *Plan, keep: Source, value: Source, ty: Type, taken: bool, origin: Instruction) res[opt[u32], refusal.Error] {
    var single: [1]Type = [1]Type{ty};
    var pair:   [2]Type = [2]Type{ty, ty};
    var by:     Source  = keep;
    if (!taken) {
        val res_not: res[bool, refusal.Error] = served_step(x, table.NOT, ty, ty, Slice[Type]{data: ?single[0], size: 1}, ty, c);
        if (sel res_not.err) { ret res[opt[u32], refusal.Error].err{res_not.err}; }
        if (!res_not.ok)     { ret res[opt[u32], refusal.Error].ok{opt[u32].none{}}; }
        val res_k: res[u32, refusal.Error] = push_step(p, Step{code: table.NOT, first: by, second: by, count: 1, lane: ty, origin: origin});
        if (sel res_k.err) { ret res[opt[u32], refusal.Error].err{res_k.err}; }
        by = Source.step{res_k.ok};
    }
    val res_and: res[bool, refusal.Error] = served_step(x, table.AND, ty, ty, Slice[Type]{data: ?pair[0], size: 2}, ty, c);
    if (sel res_and.err) { ret res[opt[u32], refusal.Error].err{res_and.err}; }
    if (!res_and.ok)     { ret res[opt[u32], refusal.Error].ok{opt[u32].none{}}; }
    val res_k: res[u32, refusal.Error] = push_step(p, Step{code: table.AND, first: value, second: by, count: 2, lane: ty, origin: origin});
    if (sel res_k.err) { ret res[opt[u32], refusal.Error].err{res_k.err}; }
    ret res[opt[u32], refusal.Error].ok{opt[u32].some{res_k.ok}};
}

# the step of an accumulator onto `p`, standing for what the branch back passes it, false where the function's code
# does not compute it packed. a conditional one combines `select(c, v, 0)` (`select(c, 0, v)` where the select takes
# the parameter where c holds), which is `and(v, m)` (`and(v, not(m))`) of `m`, the comparison's mask sign extended
# to v's lanes, all ones where c holds and zero where it does not, since zero is the operation's identity (`masked`).
# where v is a zero or sign extension of a value as wide as the lanes compared, the select is made at that width and
# extended after, since an extension of zero is zero. a sum of the constant one under c taken subtracts `m` instead,
# as a lane of all ones is minus one
fun accumulated(x: *Run, n: u32, acc: *Accesses, c: u32, p: *Plan, a: *Accumulator) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    val b:       *Body  = body_of(x);
    val lane:    Type   = b.values.data[a.param].type;
    var code:    Opcode = b.instructions.data[a.op].opcode;
    var operand: Source = source_of(p, a.other);
    if (sel operand.value && !valid(x, n, acc, a.other)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    var pair: [2]Type = [2]Type{lane, lane};
    if (a.choice != NO_INSTRUCTION) {
        val mask: Source = source_of(p, b.instructions.data[a.choice].operands.data[0]);
        if (!(sel mask.step)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        val from:    Type     = p.steps.data[mask.step].lane;
        val opt_one: opt[u64] = emit.known_in(x.c.m, b, a.other);
        var one:     bool     = false;
        if (sel opt_one.some)                        { one = opt_one.some == 1; }
        if (lane_bits(x, from) > lane_bits(x, lane)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        var narrow:  opt[Value]       = opt[Value].none{};
        var kind:    Opcode           = table.EXT_U;
        val opt_ext: opt[Instruction] = op_of(x, acc, a.other);
        if (sel opt_ext.some) {
            val de: *InstructionData = ?b.instructions.data[opt_ext.some];
            kind = de.opcode;
            if (!one && (kind == table.EXT_U || kind == table.EXT_S) && lane_bits(x, b.values.data[de.operands.data[0]].type) == lane_bits(x, from) && lane_bits(x, from) < lane_bits(x, lane)) { narrow = opt[Value].some{de.operands.data[0]}; }
        }
        if (sel narrow.some) {
            val w:   Value  = narrow.some;
            val src: Source = source_of(p, w);
            if (sel src.value && !valid(x, n, acc, w)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            val res_kept: res[opt[u32], refusal.Error] = masked(x, c, p, Source.step{mask.step}, src, b.values.data[w].type, a.taken, a.choice);
            if (sel res_kept.err)     { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_kept.err}; }
            if (sel res_kept.ok.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            val res_wide: res[opt[u32], refusal.Error] = widen(x, p, kind, Source.step{res_kept.ok.some}, b.values.data[w].type, lane, c, a.choice);
            if (sel res_wide.err)     { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_wide.err}; }
            if (sel res_wide.ok.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            operand = Source.step{res_wide.ok.some};
        }
        or {
            var wide: u32 = mask.step;
            if (lane_bits(x, from) < lane_bits(x, lane)) {
                val res_wide: res[opt[u32], refusal.Error] = widen(x, p, table.EXT_S, Source.step{wide}, from, lane, c, a.choice);
                if (sel res_wide.err)     { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_wide.err}; }
                if (sel res_wide.ok.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
                wide = res_wide.ok.some;
            }
            if (code == table.ADD && a.taken && one) {
                code    = table.SUB;
                operand = Source.step{wide};
            }
            or {
                val res_kept: res[opt[u32], refusal.Error] = masked(x, c, p, Source.step{wide}, operand, lane, a.taken, a.choice);
                if (sel res_kept.err)     { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_kept.err}; }
                if (sel res_kept.ok.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
                operand = Source.step{res_kept.ok.some};
            }
        }
    }
    val res_op: res[bool, refusal.Error] = served_step(x, code, lane, lane, Slice[Type]{data: ?pair[0], size: 2}, lane, c);
    if (sel res_op.err) { ret res_op; }
    if (!res_op.ok)     { ret res_op; }
    var first:  Source = Source.value{a.param};
    var second: Source = operand;
    if (a.choice == NO_INSTRUCTION && b.instructions.data[a.op].operands.data[0] != a.param) {
        first  = operand;
        second = Source.value{a.param};
    }
    val res_k: res[u32, refusal.Error] = push_step(p, Step{code: code, first: first, second: second, count: 2, lane: lane, origin: a.op});
    if (sel res_k.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_k.err}; }
    ret stand(p, a.result, res_k.ok);
}

# the steps of a comparison of the latch onto `p`, false where the function's code does not compute it packed: the
# comparison as the latch states it, giving a vector of conditions, and the sign extension of that mask to integer
# lanes as wide as those compared, the language's mask of all ones and zeros, which stands for the comparison's
# result. every reader of it is the select of a conditional accumulator, choosing by it
fun compared(x: *Run, n: u32, acc: *Accesses, accs: *vector.Vector[Accumulator], c: u32, p: *Plan, i: Instruction) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    val b: *Body            = body_of(x);
    val d: *InstructionData = ?b.instructions.data[i];
    if (d.operands.len != 2) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    val r:  Value      = d.results.data[0];
    val rv: *ValueData = ?b.values.data[r];
    var u:  usize      = 0;
    for (u < rv.uses.len) {
        var chooses: bool  = false;
        var a:       usize = 0;
        for (a < accs.len) {
            val ch: Instruction = accs.data[a].choice;
            if (ch != NO_INSTRUCTION && ch == rv.uses.data[u].instruction) {
                val cd: *InstructionData = ?b.instructions.data[ch];
                chooses = cd.operands.data[0] == r && cd.operands.data[1] != r && cd.operands.data[2] != r;
            }
            a = a + 1;
        }
        if (!chooses) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        u = u + 1;
    }
    val compared_type: Type = b.values.data[d.operands.data[0]].type;
    val bits:          u32  = lane_bits(x, compared_type);
    if (bits == 0) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    val res_wide: res[Type, refusal.Error] = integer_type(x, bits);
    if (sel res_wide.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_wide.err}; }
    val left:  Source = source_of(p, d.operands.data[0]);
    val right: Source = source_of(p, d.operands.data[1]);
    if (sel left.value && !valid(x, n, acc, d.operands.data[0]))  { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    if (sel right.value && !valid(x, n, acc, d.operands.data[1])) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    val res_served: res[bool, refusal.Error] = compare_served(x, d.opcode, compared_type, res_wide.ok, b.values.data[r].type, c);
    if (sel res_served.err) { ret res_served; }
    if (!res_served.ok)     { ret res_served; }
    val res_cmp: res[u32, refusal.Error] = push_step(p, Step{code: d.opcode, first: left, second: right, count: 2, lane: b.values.data[r].type, origin: i});
    if (sel res_cmp.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_cmp.err}; }
    val res_ext: res[u32, refusal.Error] = push_step(p, Step{code: table.EXT_S, first: Source.step{res_cmp.ok}, second: Source.step{res_cmp.ok}, count: 1, lane: res_wide.ok, origin: i});
    if (sel res_ext.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_ext.err}; }
    ret stand(p, r, res_ext.ok);
}

# the steps of one operation of the latch onto `p`, false where the function's code does not compute it packed
fun planned(x: *Run, n: u32, acc: *Accesses, accs: *vector.Vector[Accumulator], c: u32, p: *Plan, i: Instruction) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    val b: *Body            = body_of(x);
    val d: *InstructionData = ?b.instructions.data[i];
    var a: usize            = 0;
    for (a < accs.len) {
        val at: *Accumulator = ?accs.data[a];
        if (at.op == i && at.choice != NO_INSTRUCTION)                     { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{true}; }
        if ((at.op == i && at.choice == NO_INSTRUCTION) || at.choice == i) { ret accumulated(x, n, acc, c, p, at); }
        a = a + 1;
    }
    if (comparison(d.opcode))     { ret compared(x, n, acc, accs, c, p, i); }
    if (d.opcode == table.SELECT) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    val result: Value = d.results.data[0];
    val lane:   Type  = b.values.data[result].type;
    var srcs:   [2]Source;
    var types:  [2]Type;
    var j:      usize = 0;
    for (j < d.operands.len) {
        srcs[j] = source_of(p, d.operands.data[j]);
        if (sel srcs[j].value && !valid(x, n, acc, d.operands.data[j])) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        types[j] = source_type(x, p, srcs[j]);
        j        = j + 1;
    }
    if (conversion(d.opcode)) {
        val res_k: res[opt[u32], refusal.Error] = widen(x, p, d.opcode, srcs[0], types[0], lane, c, i);
        if (sel res_k.err)     { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_k.err}; }
        if (sel res_k.ok.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        ret stand(p, result, res_k.ok.some);
    }
    val res_served: res[bool, refusal.Error] = served_step(x, d.opcode, lane, lane, Slice[Type]{data: ?types[0], size: d.operands.len}, lane, c);
    if (sel res_served.err) { ret res_served; }
    if (!res_served.ok)     { ret res_served; }
    var second: Source = srcs[0];
    if (d.operands.len == 2) { second = srcs[1]; }
    val res_k: res[u32, refusal.Error] = push_step(p, Step{code: d.opcode, first: srcs[0], second: second, count: d.operands.len::u32, lane: lane, origin: i});
    if (sel res_k.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_k.err}; }
    ret stand(p, result, res_k.ok);
}

# whether the function's code splats a value the loop does not define that a step reads or the loop stores, at `c`
# lanes of its type, packed
fun splat_ok(x: *Run, n: u32, v: Value, c: u32) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    if (!outside(x, n, v)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{true}; }
    ret served_whole(x, table.VSPLAT, body_of(x).values.data[v].type, c);
}

# the steps of the vector loop at `c` lanes onto `into`, false where the function's code does not compute one of them
# packed: every operation of the latch in order, each splat of a value the loop does not define, each accumulator's
# reduction, and a vector of each stream's elements held in pieces
fun plan(x: *Run, n: u32, acc: *Accesses, accs: *vector.Vector[Accumulator], c: u32, into: *Plan) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    val b: *Body = body_of(x);
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < acc.loads.len + acc.stores.len) {
        var ty: Type = 0;
        if (k < acc.loads.len) { ty = b.values.data[acc.loads.data[k].value].type; }
        or                     { ty = b.values.data[acc.stores.data[k - acc.loads.len].value].type; }
        val res_piece: res[u32, refusal.Error] = piece_of(x, ty, c);
        if (sel res_piece.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_piece.err}; }
        if (res_piece.ok == 0) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    k = 0;
    for (k < acc.ops.len) {
        val res_one: res[bool, refusal.Error] = planned(x, n, acc, accs, c, into, acc.ops.data[k]);
        if (sel res_one.err) { ret res_one; }
        if (!res_one.ok)     { ret res_one; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    if (acc.stores.len == 1) {
        val v:   Value  = acc.stores.data[0].value;
        val src: Source = source_of(into, v);
        if (sel src.value && !valid(x, n, acc, v)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        val res_splat: res[bool, refusal.Error] = splat_ok(x, n, v, c);
        if (sel res_splat.err) { ret res_splat; }
        if (!res_splat.ok)     { ret res_splat; }
    }
    k = 0;
    for (k < into.steps.len) {
        val s: Step  = into.steps.data[k];
        var j: usize = 0;
        for (j < s.count::usize) {
            var src: Source = s.first;
            if (j == 1) { src = s.second; }
            if (sel src.value) {
                val res_splat: res[bool, refusal.Error] = splat_ok(x, n, src.value, c);
                if (sel res_splat.err) { ret res_splat; }
                if (!res_splat.ok)     { ret res_splat; }
            }
            j = j + 1;
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    k = 0;
    for (k < accs.len) {
        val res_reduce: res[bool, refusal.Error] = served_whole(x, accs.data[k].reduce, b.values.data[accs.data[k].param].type, c);
        if (sel res_reduce.err) { ret res_reduce; }
        if (!res_reduce.ok)     { ret res_reduce; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{true};
}

# the vector of a lane type and count
fun vector_type(x: *Run, lane: Type, lanes: u32) res[Type, refusal.Error] {
    val res_made: res[Type, type_table.Error] = type_table.intern(?x.c.m.types, type_table.Shape.vector{type_table.Vector{lanes: lanes, element: lane}});
    if (sel res_made.err) { ret res[Type, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.ir{module.Error.types{res_made.err}}}; }
    ret res[Type, refusal.Error].ok{res_made.ok};
}

# the next instructions read as `origin` and carry its flags
fun as_origin(x: *Run, st: *Site, origin: Instruction) {
    builder.derive(?st.bld, origin);
    builder.flags(?st.bld, body_of(x).instructions.data[origin].metadata.flags);
}

# a splat of `v` at `c` lanes where the loop does not define it and none was made, made where the builder is
fun splat(x: *Run, n: u32, st: *Site, v: Value, c: u32, into: *Made) err[refusal.Error] {
    val opt_made: opt[Value] = made_of(into, v);
    if (!outside(x, n, v) || sel opt_made.some) { ret err[refusal.Error].ok{}; }
    val res_vec: res[Type, refusal.Error] = vector_type(x, body_of(x).values.data[v].type, c);
    if (sel res_vec.err) { ret err[refusal.Error].err{res_vec.err}; }
    var ops:  [1]Value     = [1]Value{v};
    var imm:  [1]Immediate = [1]Immediate{Immediate.ty{res_vec.ok}};
    val wide: Value        = builder.value(?st.bld, Request{opcode: table.VSPLAT, operands: Slice[Value]{data: ?ops[0], size: 1}, immediates: Slice[Immediate]{data: ?imm[0], size: 1}, targets: Slice[Branch]{data: nil, size: 0}});
    ret note(into, v, wide);
}

# a splat of every value the loop does not define that a step reads or the loop stores, made where the builder is
fun splats(x: *Run, n: u32, st: *Site, acc: *Accesses, p: *Plan, c: u32, into: *Made) err[refusal.Error] {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < p.steps.len) {
        val s: Step  = p.steps.data[k];
        var j: usize = 0;
        for (j < s.count::usize) {
            var src: Source = s.first;
            if (j == 1) { src = s.second; }
            if (sel src.value) {
                val err_made: err[refusal.Error] = splat(x, n, st, src.value, c, into);
                if (sel err_made.err) { ret err_made; }
            }
            j = j + 1;
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    if (acc.stores.len == 1) { ret splat(x, n, st, acc.stores.data[0].value, c, into); }
    ret err[refusal.Error].ok{};
}

# the vector a source stands as: an earlier step's, or the one made of the value
fun resolved(m: *Made, formed: *Value, s: Source) opt[Value] {
    if (sel s.step) { ret opt[Value].some{formed[s.step]}; }
    ret made_of(m, s.value);
}

# the vector form of the latch's loads, the plan's steps and the store at index `at`, made where the builder is
fun lanes_body(x: *Run, st: *Site, acc: *Accesses, p: *Plan, c: u32, at: Value, into: *Made) err[refusal.Error] {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < acc.loads.len) {
        val a:       Access                   = acc.loads.data[k];
        val res_vec: res[Type, refusal.Error] = vector_type(x, body_of(x).values.data[a.value].type, c);
        if (sel res_vec.err) { ret err[refusal.Error].err{res_vec.err}; }
        builder.plain(?st.bld);
        val address: Value = element(st, a.stream, at);
        as_origin(x, st, a.at);
        var ops:       [1]Value           = [1]Value{address};
        var imm:       [2]Immediate       = [2]Immediate{Immediate.ty{res_vec.ok}, Immediate.alignment{a.stream.align}};
        val loaded:    Value              = builder.value(?st.bld, Request{opcode: table.LOAD, operands: Slice[Value]{data: ?ops[0], size: 1}, immediates: Slice[Immediate]{data: ?imm[0], size: 2}, targets: Slice[Branch]{data: nil, size: 0}});
        val err_noted: err[refusal.Error] = note(into, a.value, loaded);
        if (sel err_noted.err) { ret err_noted; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    val res_formed: res[*Value, allocator.Error] = allocator.zallocate[Value](x.a, p.steps.len + 1);
    if (sel res_formed.err) { ret err[refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_formed.err}}; }
    k = 0;
    for (k < p.steps.len) {
        val s:         Step       = p.steps.data[k];
        val opt_first: opt[Value] = resolved(into, res_formed.ok, s.first);
        val opt_other: opt[Value] = resolved(into, res_formed.ok, s.second);
        if (sel opt_first.none) { ret err[refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.reason{"a lanewise operand the vectoriser made no vector of"}}; }
        if (sel opt_other.none) { ret err[refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.reason{"a lanewise operand the vectoriser made no vector of"}}; }
        builder.derive(?st.bld, s.origin);
        var wide: Value = 0;
        if (conversion(s.code)) {
            val res_vec: res[Type, refusal.Error] = vector_type(x, s.lane, c);
            if (sel res_vec.err) { ret err[refusal.Error].err{res_vec.err}; }
            wide = emit.convert(st, s.code, opt_first.some, res_vec.ok);
        }
        or {
            var ops: [2]Value = [2]Value{opt_first.some, opt_other.some};
            wide = builder.value(?st.bld, Request{opcode: s.code, operands: Slice[Value]{data: ?ops[0], size: s.count::usize}, immediates: no_immediates(), targets: Slice[Branch]{data: nil, size: 0}});
        }
        res_formed.ok[k] = wide;
        var j: usize = 0;
        for (j < p.from.len) {
            if (p.to.data[j]::usize == k) {
                val err_noted: err[refusal.Error] = note(into, p.from.data[j], wide);
                if (sel err_noted.err) { ret err_noted; }
            }
            j = j + 1;
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    k = 0;
    for (k < acc.stores.len) {
        val a:        Access     = acc.stores.data[k];
        val opt_made: opt[Value] = made_of(into, a.value);
        if (sel opt_made.none) { ret err[refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.reason{"a stored value the vectoriser made no vector of"}}; }
        builder.plain(?st.bld);
        val address: Value = element(st, a.stream, at);
        as_origin(x, st, a.at);
        var ops: [2]Value     = [2]Value{address, opt_made.some};
        var imm: [1]Immediate = [1]Immediate{Immediate.alignment{a.stream.align}};
        builder.emit(?st.bld, Request{opcode: table.STORE, operands: Slice[Value]{data: ?ops[0], size: 2}, immediates: Slice[Immediate]{data: ?imm[0], size: 1}, targets: Slice[Branch]{data: nil, size: 0}});
        k = k + 1;
    }
    builder.plain(?st.bld);
    ret err[refusal.Error].ok{};
}

# the word a mask of the stepping parameter's bits holds with the low bits of a lane count clear
fun rounding_mask(bits: u32, lanes: u32) u64 {
    var all: u64 = ~(0::u64);
    if (bits < 64) { all = (1::u64 << bits::u64) - 1; }
    ret all & ~((lanes - 1)::u64);
}

# whether every step of a plan widens a lane or is an accumulator's own: its combine, or the comparison, mask and
# `and` a conditional one selects its value by, so the loop does no other work. such a loop that stores nothing is
# taken only at the full lane count of its narrowest lane type: without a cost model, a form of fewer lanes of a loop
# that only widens, selects and reduces is never a gain, its widening and the cut of each run costing what the scalar
# loop's whole trip does
fun reduces_only(p: *Plan, accs: *vector.Vector[Accumulator]) bool {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < p.steps.len) {
        val s:   Step  = p.steps.data[k];
        var own: bool  = conversion(s.code) || comparison(s.code);
        var a:   usize = 0;
        for (a < accs.len) {
            if (accs.data[a].choice != NO_INSTRUCTION && accs.data[a].choice == s.origin) { own = true; }
            if (accs.data[a].op == s.origin)                                              { own = true; }
            a = a + 1;
        }
        if (!own) { ret false; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret true;
}

# the narrowest lane type of the loop's elements, operations and accumulators, a condition aside, none where one is
# no type a lane is
fun narrowest(x: *Run, acc: *Accesses, accs: *vector.Vector[Accumulator]) opt[Type] {
    val b:     *Body     = body_of(x);
    var best:  opt[Type] = opt[Type].none{};
    var least: u32       = 0;
    var k:     usize     = 0;
    for (k < acc.loads.len + acc.stores.len + acc.ops.len + accs.len) {
        var ty:   Type  = 0;
        var also: Value = 0;
        var more: bool  = false;
        if (k < acc.loads.len)                  { ty = b.values.data[acc.loads.data[k].value].type; }
        or (k < acc.loads.len + acc.stores.len) { ty = b.values.data[acc.stores.data[k - acc.loads.len].value].type; }
        or (k < acc.loads.len + acc.stores.len + acc.ops.len) {
            val d: *InstructionData = ?b.instructions.data[acc.ops.data[k - acc.loads.len - acc.stores.len]];
            ty = b.values.data[d.results.data[0]].type;
            if (d.operands.len > 0) {
                also = d.operands.data[d.operands.len - 1];
                more = true;
            }
        }
        or { ty = b.values.data[accs.data[k - acc.loads.len - acc.stores.len - acc.ops.len].param].type; }
        var round: u32 = 0;
        for (round < 2) {
            if (round == 0 || more) {
                var each: Type = ty;
                if (round == 1) { each = b.values.data[also].type; }
                val bits: u32 = lane_bits(x, each);
                if (bits == 0) { ret opt[Type].none{}; }
                if (bits > 1 && (sel best.none || bits < least)) {
                    best  = opt[Type].some{each};
                    least = bits;
                }
            }
            round = round + 1;
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret best;
}

# take a lanewise loop: where a trip runs, the trips a whole number of vectors covers are at least one vector, and no
# stream it loads lies just below the one it stores (by one byte up to a vector's bytes less one, where a lane would
# read what an earlier element of its own vector wrote), a vector loop runs those trips and the loop the rest. each
# accumulator is a vector of partial values in the vector loop, every lane starting at the operation's identity, and
# its lanes are reduced and combined with what the accumulator held before the vector loop, which the header then
# takes in its place. answers whether it took the loop
fun lanes(x: *Run, n: u32, s: *Shape, acc: *Accesses) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    val b: *Body = body_of(x);
    if (acc.stores.len > 1)                      { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    if (!x.c.t.misaligned || sel x.c.basis.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    var accs:     vector.Vector[Accumulator] = vector.init[Accumulator](x.a);
    val res_accs: res[bool, refusal.Error]   = accumulators(x, s, acc, ?accs);
    if (sel res_accs.err)                     { ret res_accs; }
    if (!res_accs.ok)                         { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    if (acc.stores.len == 0 && accs.len == 0) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    val params: usize = b.blocks.data[s.head].parameters.len;
    var k:      usize = 0;
    for (k < acc.loads.len + acc.stores.len) {
        var base: Value = 0;
        if (k < acc.loads.len)         { base = acc.loads.data[k].stream.base; }
        or                             { base = acc.stores.data[k - acc.loads.len].stream.base; }
        if (!pointer_wide(x, s, base)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }

    # the lanes of a trip: the most of the narrowest lane type the widest unit holds, halved until every step is
    # computed packed, at least two, and the full count for a loop that only widens, selects and reduces
    val opt_narrow: opt[Type] = narrowest(x, acc, ?accs);
    if (sel opt_narrow.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    val res_top: res[u32, refusal.Error] = piece_of(x, opt_narrow.some, MOST);
    if (sel res_top.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_top.err}; }
    var count: u32  = res_top.ok;
    var steps: Plan = Plan{steps: vector.init[Step](x.a), from: vector.init[Value](x.a), to: vector.init[u32](x.a)};
    var found: bool = false;
    if (count < 2 || (count & (count - 1)) != 0) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    for (count >= 2 && !found) {
        steps = Plan{steps: vector.init[Step](x.a), from: vector.init[Value](x.a), to: vector.init[u32](x.a)};
        val res_plan: res[bool, refusal.Error] = plan(x, n, acc, ?accs, count, ?steps);
        if (sel res_plan.err) { ret res_plan; }
        found = res_plan.ok;
        if (!found) { count = count / 2; }
    }
    if (!found)                                                                   { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    if (count < res_top.ok && acc.stores.len == 0 && reduces_only(?steps, ?accs)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    var size: u64 = 0;
    if (acc.stores.len == 1) { size = acc.stores.data[0].stream.size; }

    # how each loaded stream lies against the stored one: apart, or at a distance that settles the test, needs none,
    # and a distance that fails it leaves the loop alone, since every run would take the element loop. streams of
    # elements of two sizes walk apart at different paces, so only two apart are taken
    var pairs: vector.Vector[usize] = vector.init[usize](x.a);
    if (acc.stores.len == 1) {
        val bits: u32 = integer_bits(x, s.word);
        k = 0;
        for (k < acc.loads.len) {
            val res_lie: res[Lie, refusal.Error] = lie_of(x, s, ?acc.stores.data[0].stream, ?acc.loads.data[k].stream);
            if (sel res_lie.err)                                                          { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_lie.err}; }
            if (acc.loads.data[k].stream.size != size && !(sel res_lie.ok.apart))         { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            if (sel res_lie.ok.at && overlaps_at(res_lie.ok.at, count::u64 * size, bits)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
            if (sel res_lie.ok.unknown) {
                val res_pushed: res[usize, allocator.Error] = vector.push[usize](?pairs, k);
                if (sel res_pushed.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_pushed.err}}; }
            }
            k = k + 1;
        }
    }

    # what the edge from outside passes the header, read before it moves
    val res_starts: res[*Value, allocator.Error] = allocator.zallocate[Value](x.a, params + 1);
    if (sel res_starts.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_starts.err}}; }
    k = 0;
    for (k < params) {
        res_starts.ok[k] = b.instructions.data[s.entering].edges.data[s.edge].arguments.data[k];
        k                = k + 1;
    }
    val starts: Slice[Value] = Slice[Value]{data: res_starts.ok, size: params};

    var st: Site = emit.init(x.c.m, x.f, b, x.a);
    fin { emit.dnit(?st); }
    var made:      Made                      = Made{from: vector.init[Value](x.a), to: vector.init[Value](x.a)};
    val res_bytes: res[Value, refusal.Error] = emit.word_constant(?st, s.word, count::u64 * size);
    if (sel res_bytes.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_bytes.err}; }

    # the origins, and the tests the streams' places do not settle, ahead of the loops whose entries fix them
    k = 0;
    for (k < acc.loads.len + acc.stores.len) {
        var err_adjusted: err[refusal.Error] = err[refusal.Error].ok{};
        if (k < acc.loads.len)    { err_adjusted = adjust(x, ?st, s, n, ?acc.loads.data[k].stream); }
        or                        { err_adjusted = adjust(x, ?st, s, n, ?acc.stores.data[k - acc.loads.len].stream); }
        if (sel err_adjusted.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{err_adjusted.err}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    var tests: vector.Vector[Value] = vector.init[Value](x.a);
    k = 0;
    for (k < pairs.len) {
        val res_over: res[Value, refusal.Error] = tested(x, ?st, s, n, ?acc.stores.data[0].stream, ?acc.loads.data[pairs.data[k]].stream, placement(x, n, no_values()), opt[Value].some{res_bytes.ok});
        if (sel res_over.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_over.err}; }
        val res_pushed: res[usize, allocator.Error] = vector.push[Value](?tests, res_over.ok);
        if (sel res_pushed.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_pushed.err}}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }

    val taken:     Block              = builder.block(?st.bld, Slice[Declaration]{data: nil, size: 0});
    val err_entry: err[refusal.Error] = entry(x, ?st, s, taken, starts);
    if (sel err_entry.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{err_entry.err}; }
    val res_mask: res[Value, refusal.Error] = emit.word_constant(?st, s.word, rounding_mask(integer_bits(x, s.word), count));
    val res_zero: res[Value, refusal.Error] = emit.word_constant(?st, s.word, 0);
    val res_step: res[Value, refusal.Error] = emit.word_constant(?st, s.word, count::u64);
    if (sel res_mask.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_mask.err}; }
    if (sel res_zero.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_zero.err}; }
    if (sel res_step.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_step.err}; }
    val whole: Value = emit.binary(?st, table.AND, trips(?st, s), res_mask.ok);
    var next:  Block = builder.block(?st.bld, Slice[Declaration]{data: nil, size: 0});
    fork(?st, emit.binary(?st, table.EQ, whole, res_zero.ok), s.head, starts, next, no_values());
    builder.at_end(?st.bld, next);
    k = 0;
    for (k < tests.len) {
        next = builder.block(?st.bld, Slice[Declaration]{data: nil, size: 0});
        fork(?st, tests.data[k], s.head, starts, next, no_values());
        builder.at_end(?st.bld, next);
        k = k + 1;
    }
    val end:        Value              = emit.binary(?st, table.ADD, s.start, whole);
    val err_splats: err[refusal.Error] = splats(x, n, ?st, acc, ?steps, count, ?made);
    if (sel err_splats.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{err_splats.err}; }

    # the vector loop's parameters: its index, then one vector per accumulator, entered at the start and the identities
    val res_decls: res[*Declaration, allocator.Error] = allocator.zallocate[Declaration](x.a, accs.len + 1);
    val res_first: res[*Value, allocator.Error]       = allocator.zallocate[Value](x.a, accs.len + 1);
    val res_again: res[*Value, allocator.Error]       = allocator.zallocate[Value](x.a, accs.len + 1);
    if (sel res_decls.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_decls.err}}; }
    if (sel res_first.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_first.err}}; }
    if (sel res_again.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_again.err}}; }
    res_decls.ok[0] = Declaration{type: s.word, secret: b.values.data[b.blocks.data[s.head].parameters.data[s.iv]].secret, name: opt[View].none{}};
    res_first.ok[0] = s.start;
    k               = 0;
    for (k < accs.len) {
        val lane:    Type                     = b.values.data[accs.data[k].param].type;
        val res_vec: res[Type, refusal.Error] = vector_type(x, lane, count);
        if (sel res_vec.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_vec.err}; }
        res_decls.ok[k + 1] = Declaration{type: res_vec.ok, secret: b.values.data[accs.data[k].param].secret, name: opt[View].none{}};
        val res_identity: res[Value, refusal.Error] = identity(x, ?st, body_of(x).instructions.data[accs.data[k].op].opcode, lane, res_vec.ok);
        if (sel res_identity.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_identity.err}; }
        res_first.ok[k + 1] = res_identity.ok;
        k                   = k + 1;
    }
    val inner: Block = builder.block(?st.bld, Slice[Declaration]{data: res_decls.ok, size: accs.len + 1});
    jump(?st, inner, Slice[Value]{data: res_first.ok, size: accs.len + 1});
    builder.at_end(?st.bld, inner);
    val at: Value = builder.parameter(?st.bld, inner, 0);
    k = 0;
    for (k < accs.len) {
        val err_noted: err[refusal.Error] = note(?made, accs.data[k].param, builder.parameter(?st.bld, inner, (k + 1)::u32));
        if (sel err_noted.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{err_noted.err}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    val err_body: err[refusal.Error] = lanes_body(x, ?st, acc, ?steps, count, at, ?made);
    if (sel err_body.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{err_body.err}; }
    val after: Value = emit.binary(?st, table.ADD, at, res_step.ok);
    res_again.ok[0] = after;
    k               = 0;
    for (k < accs.len) {
        val opt_made: opt[Value] = made_of(?made, accs.data[k].result);
        if (sel opt_made.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.reason{"an accumulator the vectoriser made no vector of"}}; }
        res_again.ok[k + 1] = opt_made.some;
        k                   = k + 1;
    }
    val tail: Block = builder.block(?st.bld, Slice[Declaration]{data: nil, size: 0});
    fork(?st, emit.binary(?st, table.NE, after, end), inner, Slice[Value]{data: res_again.ok, size: accs.len + 1}, tail, no_values());

    # the vectors' lanes reduced and combined with what each accumulator held before, the header entered with them
    builder.at_end(?st.bld, tail);
    val res_leave: res[*Value, allocator.Error] = allocator.zallocate[Value](x.a, params + 1);
    if (sel res_leave.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{res_leave.err}}; }
    res_leave.ok[s.iv] = end;
    k                  = 0;
    for (k < accs.len) {
        val a: Accumulator = accs.data[k];
        builder.derive(?st.bld, a.op);
        val code:    Opcode = body_of(x).instructions.data[a.op].opcode;
        val reduced: Value  = emit.unary(?st, a.reduce, res_again.ok[k + 1]);
        res_leave.ok[a.index] = emit.binary(?st, code, a.start, reduced);
        k                     = k + 1;
    }
    builder.plain(?st.bld);
    jump(?st, s.head, Slice[Value]{data: res_leave.ok, size: params});
    val err_built: err[refusal.Error] = emit.done(?st);
    if (sel err_built.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{err_built.err}; }
    ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{true};
}

# take loop `n` where a form of the pass applies, answering whether it did
fun take(x: *Run, ind: *Inductions, n: u32) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    var opt_shape: opt[Shape] = shape_of(x, ind, n);
    if (sel opt_shape.none) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    var s:        Shape                    = opt_shape.some;
    var acc:      Accesses                 = Accesses{loads: vector.init[Access](x.a), stores: vector.init[Access](x.a), ops: vector.init[Instruction](x.a)};
    val res_read: res[bool, refusal.Error] = accesses(x, n, ?s, ?acc);
    if (sel res_read.err) { ret res_read; }
    if (!res_read.ok)     { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    if (in_constant_time(time_of(x))) {
        if (!public_tests(x, ?s, ?acc)) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
        ret lanes(x, n, ?s, ?acc);
    }
    val res_bulk: res[bool, refusal.Error] = bulk(x, n, ?s, ?acc);
    if (sel res_bulk.err) { ret res_bulk; }
    if (res_bulk.ok)      { ret res_bulk; }
    ret lanes(x, n, ?s, ?acc);
}

# whether every value a branch the pass makes reads is public: the start, the bound, and each base and term of every
# stream
fun public_tests(x: *Run, s: *Shape, acc: *Accesses) bool {
    val b: *Body = body_of(x);
    if (b.values.data[s.start].secret || b.values.data[s.bound].secret) { ret false; }
    ret public_streams(b, ?acc.loads) && public_streams(b, ?acc.stores);
}

fun public_streams(b: *Body, list: *vector.Vector[Access]) bool {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < list.len) {
        val a: *Stream = ?list.data[k].stream;
        if (b.values.data[a.base].secret) { ret false; }
        var t: usize = 0;
        for (t < a.index.terms.len) {
            if (b.values.data[a.index.terms.data[t].value].secret) { ret false; }
            t = t + 1;
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret true;
}

# take every loop of one function a form applies to. a loop taken changes the graph, so the loops and inductions
# are read again before the next
fun visit(u: *Unit) res[bool, refusal.Error] {
    val c: *Context = u.context;
    if (c.m.functions.data[u.f].data.scalar) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{false}; }
    var ar:       arena.Arena;
    val err_made: err[allocator.Error] = arena.init(?ar, c.m.a, 0);
    if (sel err_made.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{err_made.err}}; }
    fin { arena.dnit(?ar); }
    var scratch: allocator.Allocator;
    arena.allocator(?scratch, ?ar);
    var changed: bool = false;
    var more:    bool = true;
    for (more) {
        more = false;
        arena.reset(?ar);
        val res_loops_of: res[*Loops, refusal.Error] = analysis.loops_of(c.cache, u.f);
        if (sel res_loops_of.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_loops_of.err}; }
        val res_inductions_of: res[*Inductions, refusal.Error] = analysis.inductions_of(c.cache, u.f);
        if (sel res_inductions_of.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_inductions_of.err}; }
        val res_memory_of: res[*Memory, refusal.Error] = analysis.memory_of(c.cache, u.f);
        if (sel res_memory_of.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{res_memory_of.err}; }
        var x: Run = Run{c: c, f: u.f, l: res_loops_of.ok, layout: layout.of(c.t, ?c.m.types, basis.context_of(c.basis)), mem: res_memory_of.ok, a: ?scratch};
        var n: u32 = 0;
        for (n < loops.count(x.l) && !more) {
            val res_taken: res[bool, refusal.Error] = take(?x, res_inductions_of.ok, n);
            if (sel res_taken.err) { ret res_taken; }
            if (res_taken.ok) {
                changed = true;
                more    = true;
                did(c, u.f, 1);
            }
            n = n + 1;
        }
        # the loop taken is entered from more than one place now, so it is no longer counted and is not taken again
        if (more) {
            val err_forgot: err[allocator.Error] = cache.forget(c.cache, u.f);
            if (sel err_forgot.err) { ret res[bool, refusal.Error].err{refusal.Error.alloc{err_forgot.err}}; }
        }
    }
    ret res[bool, refusal.Error].ok{changed};
}
